The idea is a daily "MAX momentum" rule built on the Birmingham paper. It goes long when the largest daily return of the last 30 days is at or above its own 150-day median and price is above the 50-day average. I took the paper''s cross-sectional coin ranking and turned it into a rule for one pair at a time. The paper gives no single-asset version.

I only read the paper''s abstract page, not the full text. I couldn''t open the Springer MAX paper, because it redirected to a login. I also left out a Donchian + Keltner breakout script from TradingView, because it is too close to the Donchian families already tried.

The file is `research/intake/S20261105T191114Z-1.json`.

Sources:
- [MAX momentum in cryptocurrency markets](https://research.birmingham.ac.uk/en/publications/max-momentum-in-cryptocurrency-markets/)','2026-11-05T19:11:14.755305+00:00');

