- `tests/test_volumespikecrashrebound_h032_v1.py`

The exit is stateless. There is no trade-state tracking, so the strategy can''t know which signal opened the position. On each bar it uses the most recent crash bar within the last 18 bars. It exits when the close reaches that bar''s open. It also exits unconditionally at bar t+18.

This can differ from the written rule when a second crash signal appears while a trade is open. The engine ignores the new entry, but the exit target then moves to the newer crash bar''s open. I judged that acceptable and didn''t change the rule.

The 4% stop is the native `stoploss = -0.04`. The 6-candle cooldown is the `protections` property.','2026-11-06T09:30:28.492365+00:00');

