Two things you might not assume:
- **Exit tracking:** the exit level is the pre-drop price `close(t-4)`, which has to be remembered per trade. I track it with a row-by-row loop in `populate_indicators` that only looks backwards. It simulates the position, the 24-bar time stop and the 12-bar cooldown.
- **Stop and cooldown mismatch:** that simulation can''t see the engine''s native 5% stop or the `CooldownPeriod` protection, which I also set to 12 candles. After a stop-out, the simulation may keep its own position open and suppress an entry signal until its own exit. This is minor and the rule is unchanged.

