Two choices where the rule left room:

- **One trade per day:** only the first qualifying breakout candle of each UTC day gets an entry signal. Freqtrade can''t see whether a trade was already taken, so I enforced the rule in the signal itself.
- **Time exit:** the exit fires on any candle opening at 19:00 UTC or later, not only the 19:00 candle. This also covers a gap in the data, so no position carries past 20:00.

The range levels carry forward only within each UTC day. A day without a 00:00 candle therefore has no range and no signals.','2026-11-06T10:06:46.681767+00:00');

