The rule is implemented as written (1h chart, daily SMA(50) uptrend gate, Sat/Sun entry signal on the 12:00 bar, exit signal on the 20:00 bar, 3% native stop, 1300 warm-up candles).

One design choice beyond the proposal''s wording: to enforce "never hold overnight," the exit signal also fires on every bar from 20:00 through 11:00 UTC. It does not fire at 12:00, so it can''t cancel that day''s entry signal. A position that survives past 21:00 for any reason is therefore closed on the next candle.','2026-11-06T12:11:27.020925+00:00');

The exit rule is a simplification of the proposal. Exits are stateless signals measured from the most recent entry signal. If a new NR7 signal appears while a position is already open, that signal is ignored for entry. It still resets the NR7-low reference and the 48-bar timer used for exits. This only matters when two entry signals fall within one hold. I did not use a stateful simulation or `custom_exit`, because both would have needed more machinery, and the first would also ignore stop-outs.

