INSERT INTO "hypotheses" VALUES('H-001','SmaTrendBaseline','SMA20/SMA50 cross, close > SMA200, stop -10%','2026-10-20T00:00:00Z','BTC/USDT 1h through 2026-10-20','frozen reference','Original result (1 trade) was a harness artifact. Re-tested 2026-11-02 under the corrected harness (exploration, BTC/ETH/BNB): rejected on all three, drawdown 44-50% at base, 74-88% at stress; lookahead and recursive pass.');
INSERT INTO "hypotheses" VALUES('H-002','DonchianBreakoutBaseline','Close > prior 20-candle high; exit below prior 10-candle low; stop -10%','2026-10-20T00:00:00Z','BTC/USDT 1h through 2026-10-20','rejected at exploration','Corrected harness, exploration on BTC/ETH/BNB: positive only at the optimistic cost, drawdown 60-98%. Do not select by return alone.');
INSERT INTO "hypotheses" VALUES('H-003','BollingerMeanReversionBaseline','Lower 20-band, RSI14 < 30, close > SMA200; exit at middle band; stop -10%','2026-10-20T00:00:00Z','BTC/USDT 1h through 2026-10-20','rejected at exploration','Not yet tested under the corrected harness. Trend-failure risk. [Audit 2026-11-04, provisional (gates.json PROPOSED), exploration only: correction: the ''not yet tested'' remark above is outdated. Re-run under the corrected harness 2026-10-30 (exploration): rejected on BTC, ETH and BNB. Base net profit BTC -14.8, ETH -19.9, BNB +48.7; profit factor 0.82/0.72/1.60. Source: research/audit/H-003-exploration-metrics.json. Protected baseline, stays in the strategy path.]');
INSERT INTO "hypotheses" VALUES('H-004','SlowTimeSeriesMomentum','Use closed 1h candles only; signals evaluated at bar close, order executed at next bar open. Long only, one position, whole balance. ENTRY: close > highest high of the prior 1440 bars (60 days, excluding current bar) AND close > SMA(4800 bars, 200 days) of close AND no open position. EXIT: close < lowest low of the prior 720 bars (30 days, excluding current bar), OR close below entry price by 15% (hard stop, checked on closed bars). After any exit, no re-entry until at least 168 bars (7 days) have passed. No other filters, no pyramiding, no take-profit.','2026-10-30T13:28:34.345485+00:00','BTC, ETH, BNB 1h through 2026-10-30; no result data viewed beyond the context file''s exploration summaries','invalid: implementation deviated from rule','Exploration ran on an implementation that used min_periods=1440 on the 4800-candle SMA (to satisfy a too-short smoke window) and without the 168-candle cooldown (backtest ran without --enable-protections). Both harness flaws are fixed. The rule itself is untested. Recorded results: research/experiments/H-004-exploration/ and the 20261030T133614Z-h-004-* manifests. Strategy file removed 2026-11-03 (implementation flawed; the 4800-bar SMA exceeds the loadable warm-up). Recoverable from git history (commit 544a3d5). [Audit 2026-11-04, provisional (gates.json PROPOSED), exploration only: classified invalid (rule untested). File removed from the strategy path without going to _archive/; documented exception, recoverable from git 544a3d5.]');
INSERT INTO "hypotheses" VALUES('H-005','VolatilitySqueezeBreakout','Closed 1h candles only; signals evaluated at bar close, order executed at next bar open. Long only, one position, whole balance. Definitions (all use completed bars): R(t) = (highest high of the 168 bars ending at t - lowest low of the 168 bars ending at t) / close(t). Squeeze(t) is true if R(t) is <= the 20th percentile of R over the 2160 bars ending at t-1 (rolling quantile 0.20, excluding the current bar). ENTRY at close of bar t when ALL hold: (1) Squeeze was true on at least one of the previous 24 bars (t-24..t-1); (2) close(t) > highest high of the prior 168 bars (t-168..t-1, excluding current bar); (3) close(t) > SMA(2400) of close; (4) no open position; (5) cooldown satisfied. EXIT at close of bar t when close(t) < lowest low of the prior 336 bars (t-336..t-1, excluding current), or via the hard stop. STOP-LOSS: fixed 8% below entry price (native intrabar stop). COOLDOWN: no re-entry for 72 candles after any exit. No take-profit, no pyramiding, no other filters. Warm-up: 2400 bars.','2026-10-30T13:49:38.324198+00:00','No price data viewed; only the context file and validation protocol (BTC, ETH, BNB 1h description through 2026-10-30).','rejected at exploration','Long breakout after a multi-day volatility squeeze in an established uptrend');
INSERT INTO "hypotheses" VALUES('H-006','RegimeGatedPullbackTrend','Closed 1h candles only; signals evaluated at bar close, order executed at next bar open. Long only, one position, whole balance. REGIME at bar t (all must hold): (a) close(t) > SMA(4800) of close; (b) SMA(2400)(t) > SMA(4800)(t); (c) SMA(4800)(t) > SMA(4800)(t-720). ENTRY at close of bar t when REGIME holds AND min(close over bars t-48..t-1) <= 0.95 * max(high over bars t-336..t-1) (a pullback of at least 5% from the 14-day high occurred within the last 48 bars) AND close(t) > SMA(48) of close AND close(t-1) <= SMA(48) at t-1 (fresh recovery cross above the 2-day mean) AND no open position AND cooldown satisfied. EXIT at close of bar t (executed next open) when any of: close(t) >= max(high over bars t-336..t-1) (prior 14-day high retested); close(t) < SMA(4800)(t) (regime lost); 240 bars have elapsed since entry (time stop). STOP-LOSS: fixed 5% below entry price (native intrabar stop). COOLDOWN: no re-entry for 48 candles after any exit. No pyramiding, no other filters. Warm-up: 5520 bars.','2026-10-30T17:42:27.332302+00:00','BTC, ETH, BNB 1h through 2026-10-20; exploration results listed in the context file only','failed','Bull-regime-only pullback re-entry with long-term slope gate and tight fixed stop Strategy file removed 2026-11-03 (never ran: warm-up 5520 > 4500). Idea re-implemented as H-010. Recoverable from git history (commit 544a3d5). [Audit 2026-11-04, provisional (gates.json PROPOSED), exploration only: classified invalid (never ran). File removed without going to _archive/; documented exception, recoverable from git 544a3d5.]');
INSERT INTO "hypotheses" VALUES('H-007','RisingTrendBreakoutGate','Closed 1h candles only; signals evaluated at bar close, order executed at next bar open. Long only, one position, whole balance. REGIME at bar t (all must hold): (a) SMA(1200)(t) > SMA(2400)(t); (b) SMA(2400)(t) > SMA(2400)(t-480) (long mean rising over the last 20 days); (c) close(t) > SMA(1200)(t). ENTRY at close of bar t when REGIME holds AND close(t) > highest high of the prior 480 bars (t-480..t-1, excluding current bar) AND no open position AND cooldown satisfied. EXIT at close of bar t (executed next open) when close(t) < lowest low of the prior 240 bars (t-240..t-1, excluding current bar) OR close(t) < SMA(1200)(t) (regime lost). STOP-LOSS: fixed 6% below entry price (native intrabar stop). COOLDOWN: no re-entry for 120 candles after any exit. No take-profit, no pyramiding, no other filters. Warm-up: 2880 bars (SMA(2400) plus 480-bar slope lag); startup_candle_count should be set to 2880 or a bit more (at most 4500) so recursive analysis is stable.','2026-10-30T18:29:04.404068+00:00','BTC, ETH, BNB 1h exploration-period summary results listed in the context file only, through 2026-10-30; no validation results seen','rejected at exploration','20-day breakout only inside a confirmed, rising multi-month uptrend, with 10-day channel exit [2026-11-03 step 0.3: has_bias on BNB traced to an 11 h data gap at 2019-05-15 03:00-12:00 plus analyzer truncation, not to the code; see research/h007-bnb-lookahead-2026-11-03.md. Decision unchanged.]');
INSERT INTO "hypotheses" VALUES('H-008','VolatilitySqueezeBreakout','Closed 1h candles only; signals evaluated at bar close, order executed at next bar open. Long only, one position, whole balance. Definitions (all use completed bars): R(t) = (highest high of the 168 bars ending at t - lowest low of the 168 bars ending at t) / close(t). Squeeze(t) is true if R(t) is <= the 20th percentile of R over the 2160 bars ending at t-1 (rolling quantile 0.20, excluding the current bar). ENTRY at close of bar t when ALL hold: (1) Squeeze was true on at least one of the previous 24 bars (t-24..t-1); (2) close(t) > highest high of the prior 168 bars (t-168..t-1, excluding current bar); (3) close(t) > SMA(2400) of close; (4) no open position; (5) cooldown satisfied. EXIT at close of bar t when close(t) < lowest low of the prior 336 bars (t-336..t-1, excluding current), or via the hard stop. STOP-LOSS: fixed 8% below entry price (native intrabar stop). COOLDOWN: no re-entry for 72 candles after any exit. No take-profit, no pyramiding, no other filters. Warm-up: 2400 bars. EXPOSURE (the only change from H-005): each trade uses 20% of the account (tradable_balance_ratio 0.20), the rest stays in cash. Rule for the number: the largest exposure on a 5% grid for which the seeded block-bootstrap (lab/bootstrap.py, block 3, 4000 resamples, seed 1) 95th-percentile closed-trade max drawdown of the H-005 exploration trades is <= 25% on BTC, ETH and BNB at once; that gives 20% (p95 20%/22%/24%; 25% gives 24%/27%/29%). Only exploration trades were used; the validation split and the final test were not read.','2026-11-02T23:39:49.008873+00:00','H-005 exploration trade lists and metrics (BTC, ETH, BNB) through 2026-10-30; no validation or final-test results seen.','not approved at validation','Exploration: candidate on BTC/ETH/BNB (drawdown 12-14%). Validation (read once, 2024-07..2026-10): profit positive on all three (+6.3/+6.9/+10.3 on 100) with drawdown 2.4-7.7%, but only 12/10/8 trades (gate needs 30, so inconclusive) and profit without the best trade negative on BTC and BNB. Not a candidate. [Audit 2026-11-04, provisional (gates.json PROPOSED), exploration only: IS->OOS base profit per day: BTC -76%, ETH -76%, BNB -82%. Exploration max drawdown on closed trades 10-13%, mark-to-market 20-30%. Source: research/audit/fase2-diagnostico.md.]');
INSERT INTO "hypotheses" VALUES('H-009','WeeklyBreakoutRegime','Closed 1h candles only; signals evaluated at bar close, order executed at next bar open. Long only, one position, whole allowed balance. REGIME at bar t: SMA(720)(t) > SMA(2160)(t) AND close(t) > SMA(720)(t). ENTRY at close of bar t when REGIME holds AND close(t) > highest high of the prior 168 bars (t-168..t-1, excluding current bar) AND no open position AND cooldown satisfied. EXIT at close of bar t (executed next open) when close(t) < lowest low of the prior 72 bars (excluding current bar) OR close(t) < SMA(720)(t). STOP-LOSS: fixed 6% below entry (native intrabar stop). COOLDOWN: 24 candles after any exit. No take-profit, no pyramiding, no other filters. Warm-up: 2160 bars. EXPOSURE: each trade uses a fixed share of the account (tradable_balance_ratio), the rest stays in cash. The share is the largest value on a 5% grid for which the seeded block-bootstrap (lab/bootstrap.py choose_exposure: block 3, 4000 resamples, seed 1) 95th-percentile closed-trade max drawdown is <= 25% on BTC, ETH and BNB at once, computed from this rule''s own exploration trades at base cost with full exposure (a calibration run, exploration split only). The value is recorded in the notes after calibration; the rule for choosing it is fixed now. If the calibration run shows fewer than 30 trades on any pair the hypothesis is dropped, not retuned. Validation split and final test not read.','2026-11-02T23:59:40.709384+00:00','Context summaries plus H-005/H-007/H-008 results and general literature (tradingstrategy.ai learn pages: Donchian/trend and moving-average timing); no result of this rule seen.','candidate at exploration','7-day breakout in a 30d/90d uptrend: more trades per year than H-007 (20-day breakout), regime gate shortened to match. Textbook horizons, no tuning. Calibrated exposure: 0.25 (p95 by pair {''BTC/USDT'': 0.11619927151132928, ''ETH/USDT'': 0.2167829050039351, ''BNB/USDT'': 0.23302999449418582}). Calibration trades: {''BTC/USDT'': 58, ''ETH/USDT'': 81, ''BNB/USDT'': 80}. [Audit 2026-11-04, provisional (gates.json PROPOSED), exploration only: classified candidate at exploration; validation NOT read. Reviewers: no lookahead or fidelity error. Caveats: largest BNB trade = 80% of profit; bootstrap 95% CI of total return includes 0 on ETH and BNB; base_2x Sharpe beats buy-and-hold and Sma200Baseline (same exposure) on BTC only; daily correlation with Sma200Baseline 0.71 on BNB; mark-to-market drawdown 11%/25%/32% vs gate 7.2%/18.5%/14.5%. research/proposals/H-009.json does not exist. Source: research/audit/H-009-exploration-metrics.json.] [Frozen for dry-run evidence collection 2026-11-04T21:39:32.190375+00:00, commit c48de4fff8, strategy sha256 c6baa8220d58; Dry-run como coleta de evidência: NÃO validada; sem evidência prospectiva; não é aprovação, não é holdout e não consome a leitura da validação.]');
INSERT INTO "hypotheses" VALUES('H-010','UptrendPullbackRecovery','Closed 1h candles only; signals evaluated at bar close, order executed at next bar open. Long only, one position, whole allowed balance. REGIME at bar t: close(t) > SMA(2400)(t) AND SMA(720)(t) > SMA(2400)(t). ENTRY at close of bar t when REGIME holds AND min(close over bars t-48..t-1) <= 0.95 * max(high over bars t-336..t-1) (a pullback of at least 5% from the 14-day high within the last 48 bars) AND close(t) > SMA(48)(t) AND close(t-1) <= SMA(48)(t-1) (fresh recovery cross) AND no open position AND cooldown satisfied. EXIT at close of bar t (executed next open) when close(t) >= max(high over bars t-336..t-1) OR close(t) < SMA(2400)(t). STOP-LOSS: fixed 5% below entry (native intrabar stop). COOLDOWN: 48 candles after any exit. No time stop, no pyramiding, no other filters. Warm-up: 2400 bars. EXPOSURE: each trade uses a fixed share of the account (tradable_balance_ratio), the rest stays in cash. The share is the largest value on a 5% grid for which the seeded block-bootstrap (lab/bootstrap.py choose_exposure: block 3, 4000 resamples, seed 1) 95th-percentile closed-trade max drawdown is <= 25% on BTC, ETH and BNB at once, computed from this rule''s own exploration trades at base cost with full exposure (a calibration run, exploration split only). The value is recorded in the notes after calibration; the rule for choosing it is fixed now. If the calibration run shows fewer than 30 trades on any pair the hypothesis is dropped, not retuned. Validation split and final test not read.','2026-11-02T23:59:40.709384+00:00','Context summaries plus H-005/H-007/H-008 results and general literature (tradingstrategy.ai learn pages: Donchian/trend and moving-average timing); no result of this rule seen.','rejected at exploration','H-006 idea (never ran: 5520-bar warm-up) with a 2400-bar long mean so it fits the 4500 limit; no time stop. Untested before. Calibrated exposure: 0.10 (p95 by pair {''BTC/USDT'': 0.17472074793385642, ''ETH/USDT'': 0.24208648328033058, ''BNB/USDT'': 0.20134252321239815}). Calibration trades: {''BTC/USDT'': 145, ''ETH/USDT'': 187, ''BNB/USDT'': 173}.');
INSERT INTO "hypotheses" VALUES('H-011','TripleBottomReversal','Closed candles only; signal at candle close, order at next open. Long only, one position, no averaging down. Pivot low at i = lowest low of [i-5,i+5] (ties allowed on the left only), KNOWN only at the close of candle i+5. Three consecutive pivot lows L1,L2,L3 (i1<i2<i3) form the support zone if (max L - min L)/mean L <= 2%, consecutive bottoms >= 12 candles apart, i3-i1 <= 150 candles. Recoveries: H1 = highest high in (i1,i2), H2 = highest high in (i2,i3); both must be >= mean bottom * 1.03. Neckline = max(H1,H2). ENTRY at the first close above the neckline at t in [i3+5, i3+5+30] and before a fourth pivot is confirmed, if no earlier close since i3 was above it, no low since i3 is below min bottom * 0.98, volume(t) >= mean volume of the previous 20 candles. Optional filters OFF in the tested rule: RSI14 higher at i3 than at i1 (positive divergence), close > EMA200. STOP at min bottom - 0.5*ATR14(t) (fixed at entry, via custom_stoploss from the signal candle). TARGET neckline + 1.0*(neckline - mean bottom). TIME STOP 150 candles. Min R/R filter configurable, OFF (0.0) because stop below support and entry at the neckline make R/R < 1 by construction. A pattern signals once and a later pattern must start after the previous signalled pattern''s last bottom (no duplicate entries). Warm-up: 800 bars. EXPOSURE: fixed share of the account chosen by the lab rule (largest 5% grid value with block-bootstrap p95 closed-trade drawdown <= 25% on all pairs, computed from this rule''s own exploration trades at base cost and full exposure; calibration run; fewer than 30 trades on a pair drops the hypothesis, no retuning). Validation and final test not read. Parameters are textbook values fixed before any result.','2026-11-03T14:11:52.700407+00:00','BTC, ETH, BNB 1h and 4h candles through 2026-10-30 (4h downloaded 2026-11-03); results of H-001..H-010 known, including the one-time validation read of H-008 (a different rule on the same 2024-07..2026-10 window) - the validation split is therefore not blind for this family of ideas. No result of THIS rule seen.','dropped: fewer than 30 trades','Triple bottom reversal, 1h. User-requested; reversal pattern, structurally R/R<1. DROPPED by the pre-registered rule: calibration trades {''BTC/USDT'': 9, ''ETH/USDT'': 5, ''BNB/USDT'': 6} (< 30 on at least one pair); not retuned.');
INSERT INTO "hypotheses" VALUES('H-012','EMASnapbackATR','Closed candles only; signal at candle close, order at next open. Long only, one position, no DCA, no martingale. z(t) = (close - EMA20)/ATR14. STRETCH: min z over the previous 6 candles (t-6..t-1) <= -2.0. ENTRY at close of t when stretch AND close(t) > EMA200(t) AND close(t) > high(t-1) (recovery confirmation) AND close(t) < EMA20(t) AND no open position AND cooldown. Optional RSI (min RSI14 over the lookback <= 35) and volume (>= mean of previous 20 candles) filters are OFF in the tested rule. STOP close(t) - 2.0*ATR14(t), fixed at entry. EXIT first close >= EMA20 (executed next open); time stop after 48 candles; alternative exit ''rr'' (1.5R target) exists as a documented option and is only an ablation. COOLDOWN 6 candles after any exit. Warm-up: 800 bars. EXPOSURE: fixed share of the account chosen by the lab rule (largest 5% grid value with block-bootstrap p95 closed-trade drawdown <= 25% on all pairs, from this rule''s own exploration trades at base cost and full exposure; fewer than 30 trades on a pair drops the hypothesis, no retuning). Validation and final test not read. Parameters are textbook values fixed before any result.','2026-11-03T14:11:52.708727+00:00','BTC, ETH, BNB 1h and 4h candles through 2026-10-30 (4h downloaded 2026-11-03); results of H-001..H-010 known, including the one-time validation read of H-008 (a different rule on the same 2024-07..2026-10 window) - the validation split is therefore not blind for this family of ideas. No result of THIS rule seen.','rejected at exploration','EMA20 ATR-normalised snapback inside an EMA200 uptrend, 1h. User-requested; mean reversion, a family that failed before (H-003). Calibrated exposure: 0.2 (p95 by pair {''BTC/USDT'': 0.14187785490232907, ''ETH/USDT'': 0.18023420143817828, ''BNB/USDT'': 0.22869875887657765}). Calibration trades: {''BTC/USDT'': 121, ''ETH/USDT'': 114, ''BNB/USDT'': 129}.');
INSERT INTO "hypotheses" VALUES('H-013','TripleBottomReversal','Closed candles only; signal at candle close, order at next open. Long only, one position, no averaging down. Pivot low at i = lowest low of [i-5,i+5] (ties allowed on the left only), KNOWN only at the close of candle i+5. Three consecutive pivot lows L1,L2,L3 (i1<i2<i3) form the support zone if (max L - min L)/mean L <= 2%, consecutive bottoms >= 12 candles apart, i3-i1 <= 150 candles. Recoveries: H1 = highest high in (i1,i2), H2 = highest high in (i2,i3); both must be >= mean bottom * 1.03. Neckline = max(H1,H2). ENTRY at the first close above the neckline at t in [i3+5, i3+5+30] and before a fourth pivot is confirmed, if no earlier close since i3 was above it, no low since i3 is below min bottom * 0.98, volume(t) >= mean volume of the previous 20 candles. Optional filters OFF in the tested rule: RSI14 higher at i3 than at i1 (positive divergence), close > EMA200. STOP at min bottom - 0.5*ATR14(t) (fixed at entry, via custom_stoploss from the signal candle). TARGET neckline + 1.0*(neckline - mean bottom). TIME STOP 150 candles. Min R/R filter configurable, OFF (0.0) because stop below support and entry at the neckline make R/R < 1 by construction. A pattern signals once and a later pattern must start after the previous signalled pattern''s last bottom (no duplicate entries). Timeframe 4h, same constants in candles. Warm-up: 800 bars. EXPOSURE: fixed share of the account chosen by the lab rule (largest 5% grid value with block-bootstrap p95 closed-trade drawdown <= 25% on all pairs, computed from this rule''s own exploration trades at base cost and full exposure; calibration run; fewer than 30 trades on a pair drops the hypothesis, no retuning). Validation and final test not read. Parameters are textbook values fixed before any result.','2026-11-03T14:11:52.712481+00:00','BTC, ETH, BNB 1h and 4h candles through 2026-10-30 (4h downloaded 2026-11-03); results of H-001..H-010 known, including the one-time validation read of H-008 (a different rule on the same 2024-07..2026-10 window) - the validation split is therefore not blind for this family of ideas. No result of THIS rule seen.','dropped: fewer than 30 trades','Same rule as H-011 on 4h candles (counts as a variant of the family). DROPPED by the pre-registered rule: calibration trades {''BTC/USDT'': 5, ''ETH/USDT'': 3, ''BNB/USDT'': 1} (< 30 on at least one pair); not retuned.');
INSERT INTO "hypotheses" VALUES('H-014','EMASnapbackATR','Closed candles only; signal at candle close, order at next open. Long only, one position, no DCA, no martingale. z(t) = (close - EMA20)/ATR14. STRETCH: min z over the previous 6 candles (t-6..t-1) <= -2.0. ENTRY at close of t when stretch AND close(t) > EMA200(t) AND close(t) > high(t-1) (recovery confirmation) AND close(t) < EMA20(t) AND no open position AND cooldown. Optional RSI (min RSI14 over the lookback <= 35) and volume (>= mean of previous 20 candles) filters are OFF in the tested rule. STOP close(t) - 2.0*ATR14(t), fixed at entry. EXIT first close >= EMA20 (executed next open); time stop after 48 candles; alternative exit ''rr'' (1.5R target) exists as a documented option and is only an ablation. COOLDOWN 6 candles after any exit. Timeframe 4h, same constants in candles. Warm-up: 800 bars. EXPOSURE: fixed share of the account chosen by the lab rule (largest 5% grid value with block-bootstrap p95 closed-trade drawdown <= 25% on all pairs, from this rule''s own exploration trades at base cost and full exposure; fewer than 30 trades on a pair drops the hypothesis, no retuning). Validation and final test not read. Parameters are textbook values fixed before any result.','2026-11-03T14:11:52.715708+00:00','BTC, ETH, BNB 1h and 4h candles through 2026-10-30 (4h downloaded 2026-11-03); results of H-001..H-010 known, including the one-time validation read of H-008 (a different rule on the same 2024-07..2026-10 window) - the validation split is therefore not blind for this family of ideas. No result of THIS rule seen.','dropped: fewer than 30 trades','Same rule as H-012 on 4h candles (counts as a variant of the family). DROPPED by the pre-registered rule: calibration trades {''BTC/USDT'': 33, ''ETH/USDT'': 27, ''BNB/USDT'': 32} (< 30 on at least one pair); not retuned.');
INSERT INTO "hypotheses" VALUES('H-015','TimeSeriesMomentum','Closed DAILY candles (Freqtrade informative 1d merged with merge_informative_pair), executed on 1h at the next open. Long only, one position, whole allowed balance, no stop-loss, no sizing hooks. mom(d) = close(d)/close(d-N days) - 1. ENTRY while mom > 0 (and, with the regime, regime_on() true = daily close > SMA(200); vol_regime off per the step-1.4 ablation). EXIT when mom <= 0 (or the regime turns off). GRID (pre-declared, complete): N in {30, 60, 90, 120, 180} x regime in {off, on} = 10 configurations; N_trials for the DSR = 10. Each configuration is also a test at costs base and base_2x on each of BTC, ETH, BNB. Warm-up 400 bars (daily and 1h). PASS CRITERIA TO READ VALIDATION (fixed before running, all required): DSR of the best configuration (N=10) >= 0.95; PBO (CSCV, 16 slices) <= 0.5; plateau (neighbouring N with the same regime flag reach >= 70% of the best Sharpe); Sharpe above buy-and-hold AND above Sma200Baseline at base_2x in the IS; >= 30 trades per pair; lab/config/gates.json clear on exploration. Fail = family rejected and archived. The validation split is then read ONCE, for the configuration chosen in the IS. Final test / prospective holdout not read.','2026-11-04T00:11:34.975802+00:00','BTC, ETH, BNB 1h/4h/1d candles through 2026-11-02; results of H-001..H-014 known, including the one-time validation read of H-008 and the Sma200Baseline cycle table (so the validation window is not blind for trend-following ideas). No result of THIS rule seen. Regime-filter ablation (IS only) known.','rejected (family): configuration H-016 not approved at validation','Step 2, family 1 of 3 (TSMOM). Pre-registered grid of 10; textbook horizons. [2026-11-03 grid explored on the IS (research/grids/H-015-exploration.json): best N30_noreg; DSR 0.999, PBO 0.31, plateau pass, beats B&H and Sma200 at base_2x, >= 89 trades per pair; selected cell registered as H-016.]');
INSERT INTO "hypotheses" VALUES('H-016','TimeSeriesMomentum','Same rule as H-015 with N_DAYS = 30 and no regime filter (the H-015 grid winner at base_2x in the exploration split: pooled Sharpe 1.49 vs buy-and-hold 1.15 and Sma200Baseline 1.05; DSR(N=10) 0.999; PBO 0.31; plateau 0.83 of the best at N=60). Closed daily candles via merge_informative_pair, executed on 1h at the next open; long only, one position, no stop-loss, no sizing hooks. ENTRY while close(d)/close(d-30) > 1; EXIT when it is <= 1. N_trials inherited from H-015 = 10 (this is not a new draw: it is the selected cell of that grid; the family counts 11 registered hypotheses). Exposure: fixed share chosen by the lab rule (largest 5% value with block-bootstrap p95 closed-trade drawdown <= 25% on all pairs, from this rule''s own exploration trades at base cost and full exposure). Gates of lab/config/gates.json on exploration; only if all clear, the validation split is read ONCE. Final test / prospective holdout not read.','2026-11-04T00:34:35.725730+00:00','Same as H-015 plus the full exploration grid of H-015 (which is where this configuration was chosen). The validation split has not been read for this rule; it was read once for H-008 (a different rule).','not approved at validation','Child of H-015. Winner at the grid edge (N=30, the shortest horizon): the plateau test has one neighbour only. Calibrated exposure: 0.15 (p95 by pair {''BTC/USDT'': 0.19407518252890127, ''ETH/USDT'': 0.15886218231018612, ''BNB/USDT'': 0.20444195374091295}). Calibration trades: {''BTC/USDT'': 94, ''ETH/USDT'': 89, ''BNB/USDT'': 96}. [Validation read once (exposure 0.15): BTC rejected (profit ex-best trade -5.2), ETH candidate, BNB rejected (ex-best -3.2). Report: research/grids/H-015-report.md. Code archived.] [Audit 2026-11-04, provisional (gates.json PROPOSED), exploration only: IS->OOS base profit per day: BTC -96%, ETH -63%, BNB -96%. Exploration cross-pair consistency (min/max profit per day) 0.22, below the 0.25 portfolio minimum. Mark-to-market drawdown 24%/25%/48% vs gate 14.0%/11.4%/9.7%. Source: research/audit/fase2-diagnostico.md.] [Frozen for dry-run evidence collection 2026-11-05T17:29:09.726808+00:00, commit 6d59a5711a, strategy sha256 456e194f571e; Dry-run como coleta de evidência: NÃO validada; sem evidência prospectiva; não é aprovação, não é holdout e não consome a leitura da validação.]');
INSERT INTO "hypotheses" VALUES('H-017','WeeklyBreakoutRegime','Closed 1h candles only; signals evaluated at bar close, order executed at next bar open. Long only, one position, whole allowed balance (same exposure rule as H-009). Identical to H-009 except for ONE added regime condition. REGIME at bar t: SMA(720)(t) > SMA(2160)(t) AND close(t) > SMA(720)(t) AND SMA(2160)(t) > SMA(2160)(t-720) (the 90-day mean is higher than it was 30 days ago, i.e. the slow trend is rising). ENTRY at close of bar t when REGIME holds AND close(t) > highest high of the prior 168 bars (t-168..t-1, excluding current bar) AND no open position AND cooldown satisfied. EXIT at close of bar t (executed next open) when close(t) < lowest low of the prior 72 bars (excluding current bar) OR close(t) < SMA(720)(t). STOP-LOSS: fixed 6% below entry price (native intrabar stop). COOLDOWN: no re-entry for 24 candles after any exit. No take-profit, no pyramiding, no other filters. The slope lag of 720 bars is fixed ex ante (30 days); no other value is run, the grid is the single cell {720}, with H-009 (no slope condition) as the reference. Warm-up: 2880 bars.','2026-11-04T13:36:02.214749+00:00','Context file research/context/H-017.md with exploration-only audit facts for H-009; no price data, validation or final test results were viewed.','rejected at exploration','Weekly breakout gated by a rising 90-day mean to avoid post-peak failed breakouts Calibrated exposure: 0.3 (p95 by pair {''BTC/USDT'': 0.17130307434664505, ''ETH/USDT'': 0.24866607440735666, ''BNB/USDT'': 0.19669332877281875}). Calibration trades: {''BTC/USDT'': 54, ''ETH/USDT'': 70, ''BNB/USDT'': 62}. [Audit 2026-11-04, provisional (gates.json PROPOSED), exploration only: rejected at exploration. ETH failed the gate on max drawdown at the stress cost (25.5% > 25%) at the rule-calibrated exposure 0.3; BTC and BNB passed. Paired against H-009 on the same window and costs: daily-return correlation 0.86 (BTC) / 0.89 (ETH) / 0.98 (BNB); H-017 in-position time lies 100% inside H-009''s; base_2x Sharpe at exposure 0.3: 0.78 vs 1.12 (BTC), 0.54 vs 0.58 (ETH), 0.64 vs 0.61 (BNB); redundant. Longest losing streak fell (9->7, 14->11, 11->6) but the mark-to-market drawdown barely changed (H-017 12%/27%/34% vs H-009 at the same exposure 13%/29%/34%). Single-cell grid by design: DSR, PBO and plateau not computed. Validation not read. Source: research/audit/H-017-exploration-metrics.json, H-009x30-exploration-metrics.json. Archived.]');
INSERT INTO "hypotheses" VALUES('H-018','DonchianEnsemble','Protocol docs/protocolo-validacao-v3.md section 2.2. Signals come from CLOSED daily candles (merge_informative_pair, ffill, as in Sma200Baseline) and are executed on the 1h chart at the next open. Four members (N, M) = (20,10), (55,20), (100,50), (200,100). Member state is a two-level latch computed on the daily frame: ON when daily close > max(daily high of the N days before the current day) ; OFF when daily close < min(daily low of the M days before the current day) ; otherwise the previous state is kept ; undefined (NaN) channel values give OFF. Channels use rolling(N).max().shift(1) and rolling(M).min().shift(1) on the daily frame before the merge. ENTRY: at least 2 of the 4 members are ON and the strategy is flat (level entry, including the first candle of a split if already ON). EXIT: fewer than 2 members ON. No stop-loss (stoploss attribute -0.99 only to satisfy the engine contract), no take-profit, no sizing hooks, no cooldown. Exposure is the fixed share chosen by the lab rule (bootstrap.choose_exposure on exploration trades). Sensitivities reported, never selectable: threshold 1 and 3 of 4, each member alone, the vote without member (20,10), thresholds counted in the DSR N. Warm-up: 400 bars (daily candles; the state at the first day of a split was verified equal to the full-history state for 400, 600 and 900 days on BTC, ETH and BNB).','2026-11-04T18:26:46.153196+00:00','Protocol v3 and exploration-only audit facts; no validation or holdout result was used for this rule.','dropped: fewer than 30 trades','Donchian ensemble: majority vote of four daily channels, no stop. Protocol v3 (docs/protocolo-validacao-v3.md); decisions D-1..D-10 per the user''s 2026-11-04 ''use all proposals''; gates.json/portfolio.json still PROPOSED, so every decision is provisional. DROPPED by the pre-registered rule: calibration trades {''BTC/USDT'': 17, ''ETH/USDT'': 14, ''BNB/USDT'': 16} (< 30 on at least one pair); not retuned. [Smoke, lookahead and recursive clean on BTC, ETH, BNB before the calibration. Result: inconclusive by the 30-trade rule (protocol D-2 kept); no gate decision, no validation read, no sensitivity run. Archived. Consequence: the Donchian family cannot be evaluated at daily horizons under the current gate; any change of the 30-trade rule is a user decision (D-2) and cannot be made after seeing this result for H-018.]');
INSERT INTO "hypotheses" VALUES('H-019','DailyRSI2Dip','Signals use CLOSED DAILY candles (UTC) built from the 1h data (Freqtrade informative 1d merged with merge_informative_pair, forward-filled, so a daily value is visible only after that day has closed); orders execute on the 1h chart at the next 1h open. Long only, one position, whole allowed balance, no pyramiding, no profit target, no sizing hooks. Indicators on daily closes: RSI(2) with Wilder smoothing (alpha = 1/2, seeded with the simple average of the first 2 changes); SMA(200 days); SMA(5 days). ENTRY when a daily candle closes with: daily close > SMA(200) AND RSI(2) < 10 AND no open position. EXIT when a daily candle closes with: daily close > SMA(5) OR daily close < SMA(200). STOP-LOSS: none in the rule (published exit only); the strategy sets stoploss = -0.99 only to satisfy the engine contract, never a binding stop. No cooldown. No other filters. Exposure: fixed share of the account chosen by the lab rule (largest 5% grid value with block-bootstrap p95 closed-trade drawdown <= 25% on all pairs, from this rule''s own exploration trades at base cost and full exposure; fewer than 30 trades on a pair drops the hypothesis, no retuning). All numbers fixed ex ante from the published rule: RSI length 2, threshold 10, exit average 5 days, trend average 200 days; no grid. Warm-up: 400 bars (daily candles on the informative frame: 200 for SMA(200) plus 200 for Wilder RSI to stabilise; the 1h startup_candle_count is set to 400 as in H-015/H-018, well under the 4500 limit).','2026-11-04T21:41:04.194059+00:00','No price data seen; only research/context/H-019.md exploration-level summaries and the protocol; BTC, ETH, BNB 1h through 2026-11-04 exist but were not inspected.','rejected at exploration','Daily RSI(2) oversold dip buy inside a 200-day uptrend, exit above 5-day SMA Calibrated exposure: 0.2 (p95 by pair {''BTC/USDT'': 0.17410420469738616, ''ETH/USDT'': 0.21622252679628054, ''BNB/USDT'': 0.15089732849803617}). Calibration trades: {''BTC/USDT'': 53, ''ETH/USDT'': 54, ''BNB/USDT'': 57}.');
INSERT INTO "hypotheses" VALUES('H-020','Double7ChannelDip','Signals use CLOSED DAILY candles (UTC) built from the 1h data (Freqtrade informative 1d merged with merge_informative_pair, forward-filled, so a daily value is visible only after that day has closed); orders execute on the 1h chart at the next 1h open. Long only, one position per pair, whole allowed balance, no pyramiding, no profit target, no time exit, no sizing hooks, no cooldown, no other filters. Indicators on daily closes: SMA(200 days) of daily close; lowest daily close of the last 7 days INCLUDING the current (just closed) day; highest daily close of the last 7 days INCLUDING the current day. ENTRY when a daily candle closes with: daily close > SMA(200) AND daily close <= lowest daily close of the last 7 days (including that day) AND no open position. EXIT when a daily candle closes with: daily close >= highest daily close of the last 7 days (including that day). STOP-LOSS: none in the published rule; the strategy sets stoploss = -0.99 only to satisfy the engine contract, never a binding stop. Lookbacks: 7 days entry channel, 7 days exit channel, 200 days trend filter; no grid, no tuning. Exposure: fixed share of the account chosen by the lab rule (largest 5% grid value with block-bootstrap p95 closed-trade drawdown <= 25% on all pairs, from this rule''s own exploration trades at base cost and full exposure; fewer than 30 trades on a pair drops the hypothesis, no retuning). Warm-up: 400 bars (daily candles on the informative frame: 200 for the SMA(200) plus 200 spare; startup_candle_count 400 as in H-015/H-019, under the 4500 limit).','2026-11-05T15:45:17.012151+00:00','No price data viewed; only the research context file (hypothesis list and exploration summaries) and the validation protocol; BTC, ETH, BNB 1h data not inspected.','not approved at validation','Daily Double 7: buy a 7-day closing low above the 200-day mean, sell a 7-day closing high Calibrated exposure: 0.1 (p95 by pair {''BTC/USDT'': 0.07103916095809959, ''ETH/USDT'': 0.21304422295439313, ''BNB/USDT'': 0.16275232274666154}). Calibration trades: {''BTC/USDT'': 58, ''ETH/USDT'': 66, ''BNB/USDT'': 64}.');
INSERT INTO "hypotheses" VALUES('H-021','DailyIBSDip','Signals use CLOSED DAILY candles (UTC) built from the 1h data (Freqtrade informative 1d merged with merge_informative_pair, forward-filled, so a daily value is visible only after that day has closed); orders execute on the 1h chart at the next 1h open. Long only, one position per pair, whole allowed balance, no pyramiding, no profit target, no time exit, no sizing hooks, no other filters. Daily IBS = (close - low) / (high - low) of the closed daily candle; days with high == low are skipped (no signal, state unchanged). SMA200 = simple mean of the last 200 daily closes including the just-closed day. ENTRY when a daily candle closes with IBS < 0.2 AND daily close > SMA200 AND no open position. EXIT (first that occurs) when a later daily candle closes with IBS >= 0.8, OR a daily candle closes below SMA200 (safety exit), OR the hard stop. STOP-LOSS: one fixed 12% below the entry price (native intrabar stop). COOLDOWN: none. All numbers fixed ex ante, no grid: IBS entry threshold 0.2, IBS exit threshold 0.8, trend mean 200 days, stop 12%. Exposure: fixed share of the account chosen by the lab rule (largest 5% grid value with block-bootstrap p95 closed-trade drawdown <= 25% on all pairs, from this rule''s own exploration trades at base cost and full exposure; fewer than 30 trades on a pair drops the hypothesis, no retuning). Warm-up: 400 bars (daily candles on the informative frame: 200 for the SMA200 plus 200 spare; startup_candle_count 400 as in H-015/H-019/H-020, under the 4500 limit).','2026-11-05T17:23:13.785085+00:00','No price data viewed; only the research context file with exploration-level summaries of earlier hypotheses (data up to 2026-11-05 not inspected).','failed: causality checks','Daily internal bar strength dip buy inside a 200-day uptrend');
INSERT INTO "hypotheses" VALUES('H-022','ThreeDayLowerRangeDip','Signals use CLOSED DAILY candles (UTC) built from the 1h data (Freqtrade informative 1d merged with merge_informative_pair, forward-filled, so a daily value is visible only after that day has closed); orders execute on the 1h chart at the next 1h open. Long only, one position per pair, whole allowed balance, no pyramiding, no add-ons, no profit target, no time exit, no sizing hooks, no cooldown, no other filters. Indicators on daily data: SMA(200) of daily close and SMA(5) of daily close, both including the just-closed day. Let H(d), L(d) be the daily high and low of day d, d = the just-closed day. THREE-DAY FALLING RANGE: H(d)<H(d-1) AND L(d)<L(d-1) AND H(d-1)<H(d-2) AND L(d-1)<L(d-2) AND H(d-2)<H(d-3) AND L(d-2)<L(d-3) (strict inequalities). ENTRY when a daily candle closes with: close(d) > SMA200(d) AND close(d) < SMA5(d) AND the three-day falling range holds AND no open position. EXIT (first that occurs): a daily candle closes above SMA5; OR a daily candle closes below SMA200 (safety exit); OR the hard stop. STOP-LOSS: one fixed 12% below the entry price (native intrabar stop). COOLDOWN: none. All numbers fixed ex ante from the published method, no grid: 200-day trend mean, 5-day exit/entry mean, 3 falling days, 12% stop. Exposure: fixed share of the account chosen by the lab rule (largest 5% grid value with block-bootstrap p95 closed-trade drawdown <= 25% on all pairs, from this rule''s own exploration trades at base cost and full exposure; fewer than 30 trades on a pair drops the hypothesis, no retuning). Warm-up: 400 bars (daily candles on the informative frame: 200 for SMA(200) plus 200 spare; startup_candle_count 400 as in H-015/H-019/H-020/H-021, under the 4500 limit).','2026-11-05T18:40:32.938103+00:00','No price data seen. Only research/context/H-022.md (exploration-split summaries of earlier hypotheses) and research/validation-protocol-v2.md; BTC, ETH, BNB 1h.','dropped: fewer than 30 trades','Connors 3-day lower highs and lows pullback inside a 200-day uptrend (daily signals, 1h execution) DROPPED by the pre-registered rule: calibration trades {''BTC/USDT'': 25, ''ETH/USDT'': 31, ''BNB/USDT'': 32} (< 30 on at least one pair); not retuned.');
INSERT INTO "hypotheses" VALUES('H-023','DailyR3Streak','Signals use CLOSED DAILY candles (UTC) built from the 1h data (Freqtrade informative 1d merged with merge_informative_pair, forward-filled, so a daily value is visible only after that day has closed); orders execute on the 1h chart at the next 1h open. Long only, one position per pair, whole allowed balance, no pyramiding, no profit target, no time exit, no sizing hooks, no cooldown, no other filters. Indicators on daily closes: RSI(2) with Wilder smoothing (alpha = 1/2, seeded with the simple average of the first 2 changes); SMA(200 days) including the just-closed day. Let RSI(0) be the RSI of the just-closed day d, RSI(1), RSI(2), RSI(3) the values 1, 2, 3 days earlier. ENTRY when a daily candle closes with: close(d) > SMA200(d) AND RSI(0) < RSI(1) AND RSI(1) < RSI(2) AND RSI(2) < RSI(3) (strict, three consecutive falls) AND RSI(3) < 60 AND RSI(0) < 10 AND no open position. EXIT when a daily candle closes with RSI(0) > 70. STOP-LOSS: none in the published rule; the strategy sets stoploss = -0.99 only to satisfy the engine contract, never a binding stop. No cooldown. All numbers fixed ex ante from the published rule, no grid: RSI length 2, entry threshold 10, prior-reading cap 60, exit threshold 70, 3 falling days, trend mean 200 days. Exposure: fixed share of the account chosen by the lab rule (largest 5% grid value with block-bootstrap p95 closed-trade drawdown <= 25% on all pairs, from this rule''s own exploration trades at base cost and full exposure; fewer than 30 trades on a pair drops the hypothesis, no retuning). Warm-up: 400 bars (daily candles on the informative frame: 200 for SMA(200) plus 200 for the Wilder RSI to stabilise; the 1h startup_candle_count is set to 400 as in H-015/H-019/H-020, well under the 4500 limit).','2026-11-05T18:56:37.346980+00:00','No price data inspected; only the context file''s exploration summaries of earlier hypotheses (BTC, ETH, BNB 1h, exploration split) through 2026-11-05.','dropped: fewer than 30 trades','Daily R3: three falling RSI(2) days ending below 10 in a 200-day uptrend DROPPED by the pre-registered rule: calibration trades {''BTC/USDT'': 18, ''ETH/USDT'': 20, ''BNB/USDT'': 22} (< 30 on at least one pair); not retuned.');
INSERT INTO "hypotheses" VALUES('H-024','DailyMaxJumpMomentum','Signals use CLOSED DAILY candles (UTC) built from the 1h data (informative 1d merged with merge_informative_pair, forward-filled, so a daily value is visible only after that day has closed); orders execute on the 1h chart at the next 1h open. Long only, one position per pair, whole allowed balance, no pyramiding, no profit target, no other filters. Definitions on daily closes C(d), d = just-closed day: r(d) = C(d)/C(d-1) - 1. MAX(d) = largest r over the 30 most recent daily returns r(d-29..d), including the just-closed day. Jump regime is ON when MAX(d) >= median of the 150 values MAX(d-150..d-1) (excluding today). SMA50 = mean of the last 50 daily closes including d; SMA20 = mean of the last 20 daily closes including d. ENTRY when a daily candle closes with: jump regime ON AND C(d) > SMA50(d) AND C(d) > highest daily close of the 10 days d-10..d-1 (excluding d) AND no open position AND cooldown satisfied. EXIT when a daily candle closes with C(d) < SMA20(d), or via the hard stop. STOP-LOSS: one fixed 12% below the entry price (native intrabar stop, not a closed-bar check). COOLDOWN: no re-entry for 72 candles (3 days) after any exit. No grid; all numbers fixed ex ante: 30-day MAX window, 150-day median window, median threshold, 50-day trend mean, 10-day breakout, 20-day exit mean, 12% stop, 3-day cooldown. Exposure: fixed share of the account chosen by the lab rule (largest 5% grid value with block-bootstrap p95 closed-trade drawdown <= 25% on all pairs, from this rule''s own exploration trades at base cost and full exposure; fewer than 30 trades on a pair drops the hypothesis, no retuning). Warm-up: 4400 bars (longest daily chain is 1 return + 29 more for MAX plus 150 for the median = about 180 days = 4320 hourly bars, plus one partial day of margin; startup_candle_count 4400, under the 4500 limit).','2026-11-05T19:12:28.530245+00:00','No price data seen; only the context file research/context/H-024.md with exploration-split summary results of earlier hypotheses (BTC, ETH, BNB 1h, exploration only; validation and final test not read).','not approved at validation','Daily lottery-jump (MAX) persistence gate with 20-day mean exit Calibrated exposure: 0.25 (p95 by pair {''BTC/USDT'': 0.16914283121968346, ''ETH/USDT'': 0.15549983612983403, ''BNB/USDT'': 0.22363946613512}). Calibration trades: {''BTC/USDT'': 43, ''ETH/USDT'': 36, ''BNB/USDT'': 39}.');
INSERT INTO "hypotheses" VALUES('H-025','DailyKeltnerBreakout','Signals use CLOSED DAILY candles (UTC) built from the 1h data (informative 1d merged with merge_informative_pair, forward-filled, so a daily value is visible only after that day has closed); orders execute on the 1h chart at the next 1h open. Long only, one position per pair, whole allowed balance, no pyramiding, no profit target, no sizing hooks, no cooldown, no other filters. Daily indicators (d = just-closed day, included): EMA20 = EMA of daily close, span 20 (alpha 2/21), seeded with the first daily close; TR(d) = max(high-low, |high-close(d-1)|, |low-close(d-1)|); ATR20 = Wilder smoothing of TR (alpha 1/20, seeded with the mean of the first 20 TRs); UpperBand(d) = EMA20(d) + 1.5*ATR20(d); SMA100 = mean of the last 100 daily closes including d. ENTRY when a daily candle closes with: close(d) > UpperBand(d) AND close(d-1) <= UpperBand(d-1) (fresh cross) AND close(d) > SMA100(d) AND no open position. EXIT when a daily candle closes with close(d) < EMA20(d), or via the hard stop. STOP-LOSS: one fixed 8% below the entry price (native intrabar stop); about 2 daily ATRs of these pairs, not tuned. No grid; all numbers fixed ex ante: EMA length 20, ATR length 20, band multiplier 1.5, trend mean 100 days, stop 8%. Exposure: fixed share of the account chosen by the lab rule (largest 5% grid value with block-bootstrap p95 closed-trade drawdown <= 25% on all pairs, from this rule''s own exploration trades at base cost and full exposure; fewer than 30 trades on a pair drops the hypothesis, no retuning). Warm-up: 3700 bars (150 daily candles = 3600 hourly bars plus one partial day and margin: 100 days for SMA100, and about 130 days for EMA20 and Wilder ATR20 to forget their seeds; startup_candle_count 3700, under the 4500 limit).','2026-11-05T19:40:05.035504+00:00','No price data was viewed. Exploration-split summary results of earlier hypotheses (H-001 to H-024) in the context file only; no validation or final-test data.','not approved at validation','Daily Keltner upper-band close breakout in uptrend, exit at daily EMA20 Calibrated exposure: 0.2 (p95 by pair {''BTC/USDT'': 0.12562327750912983, ''ETH/USDT'': 0.0978692427772229, ''BNB/USDT'': 0.23838007584618998}). Calibration trades: {''BTC/USDT'': 33, ''ETH/USDT'': 33, ''BNB/USDT'': 41}.');
INSERT INTO "hypotheses" VALUES('H-026','NearHighAnchorGate','Signals use CLOSED DAILY candles (UTC) built from the 1h data (informative 1d merged with merge_informative_pair, forward-filled, so a daily value is visible only after that day has closed); orders execute on the 1h chart at the next 1h open. Long only, one position per pair, whole allowed balance, no pyramiding, no take-profit, no sizing hooks, no cooldown, no other filters. Definitions on daily candles, d = just-closed day: H(d) = highest daily HIGH of the 182 daily candles ending at d (d included). N(d) = close(d) / H(d). ENTRY when a daily candle closes with N(d) >= 0.95 AND no position is open. EXIT when a daily candle closes with N(d) < 0.85. While 0.85 <= N(d) < 0.95 the current state is held (hysteresis: no entry, no exit). STOP-LOSS: none in the rule; the strategy sets stoploss = -0.99 only to satisfy the engine contract, never a binding stop (the 0.85 exit is the risk control). If H(d) is undefined (fewer than 182 daily candles) no signal. All numbers fixed ex ante, no grid: window 182 days, entry 0.95, exit 0.85. Exposure: fixed share of the account chosen by the lab rule (largest 5% grid value with block-bootstrap p95 closed-trade drawdown <= 25% on all pairs, from this rule''s own exploration trades at base cost and full exposure; fewer than 30 trades on a pair drops the hypothesis, no retuning). Warm-up: 4400 bars (182 daily candles = 4368 hourly bars plus a partial day of margin; under the 4500 limit).','2026-11-05T20:08:41.257475+00:00','Context file research/context/H-026.md only (exploration-split summaries); no price data and no validation or final-test results were viewed.','dropped: fewer than 30 trades','Daily nearness-to-26-week-high anchoring gate with hysteresis exit DROPPED by the pre-registered rule: calibration trades {''BTC/USDT'': 16, ''ETH/USDT'': 19, ''BNB/USDT'': 17} (< 30 on at least one pair); not retuned.');
INSERT INTO "hypotheses" VALUES('H-027','DailySupertrendFlip','Signals use CLOSED DAILY candles (UTC) built from the 1h data (informative 1d merged with merge_informative_pair, forward-filled, so a daily value is visible only after that day has closed); orders execute on the 1h chart at the next 1h open. Long only, one position per pair, whole allowed balance, no pyramiding, no take-profit, no sizing hooks, no cooldown, no other filters. Daily definitions (d = just-closed day, included): TR(d) = max(high-low, |high-close(d-1)|, |low-close(d-1)|); ATR(d) = Wilder smoothing of TR with length 10 (alpha 1/10, seeded with the mean of the first 10 TRs); hl2 = (high+low)/2; BasicUpper = hl2 + 3.0*ATR; BasicLower = hl2 - 3.0*ATR. FinalUpper(d) = BasicUpper(d) if BasicUpper(d) < FinalUpper(d-1) or close(d-1) > FinalUpper(d-1), else FinalUpper(d-1). FinalLower(d) = BasicLower(d) if BasicLower(d) > FinalLower(d-1) or close(d-1) < FinalLower(d-1), else FinalLower(d-1). Trend state: initial state is DOWN on the first day with a defined ATR. If state(d-1) is DOWN and close(d) > FinalUpper(d) the state becomes UP; if state(d-1) is UP and close(d) < FinalLower(d) the state becomes DOWN; otherwise it is unchanged. The Supertrend line is FinalLower in UP and FinalUpper in DOWN. ENTRY when a daily candle closes and the state flips from DOWN to UP on that day, and no position is open (flip only; a state that is already UP is not an entry, including on the first candle of a split). EXIT when a daily candle closes and the state flips from UP to DOWN (daily close below the Supertrend line). STOP-LOSS: none in the rule; the strategy sets stoploss = -0.99 only to satisfy the engine contract, never a binding stop (the Supertrend line is the trailing exit, evaluated on daily closes). No cooldown. All numbers fixed ex ante, no grid: ATR length 10, multiplier 3.0. Exposure: fixed share of the account chosen by the lab rule (largest 5% grid value with block-bootstrap p95 closed-trade drawdown <= 25% on all pairs, from this rule''s own exploration trades at base cost and full exposure; fewer than 30 trades on a pair drops the hypothesis, no retuning). Warm-up: 3700 bars (150 daily candles = 3600 hourly bars plus a partial day and margin, so the Wilder ATR seed and the ratcheting bands forget their start; under the 4500 limit).','2026-11-05T20:27:07.052658+00:00','Only the context file research/context/H-027.md (exploration-split summaries of earlier hypotheses) and the validation protocol; no validation or final-test results; no price data inspected.','dropped: fewer than 30 trades','Daily Supertrend (ATR 10, x3) long-only flip trend follower on 1h execution DROPPED by the pre-registered rule: calibration trades {''BTC/USDT'': 26, ''ETH/USDT'': 24, ''BNB/USDT'': 20} (< 30 on at least one pair); not retuned.');
INSERT INTO "hypotheses" VALUES('H-028','IntradayEarlySessionMomentum','Closed 1h candles only, UTC clock; signals evaluated at bar close, orders executed at the next bar open. Long only, one position per pair, whole allowed balance, no pyramiding, no take-profit, no sizing hooks, no other filters. DEFINITION: for each UTC day, O0 = open of the 00:00 UTC bar; C3 = close of the 03:00 UTC bar (the bar covering 03:00-04:00); r = C3 / O0 - 1. ENTRY: at the close of the 03:00 UTC bar, if r >= 0.01 and no position is open, buy at the open of the next bar (04:00 UTC). If the 00:00 or 03:00 bar is missing, no signal that day. EXIT: at the close of the 15:00 UTC bar (the bar covering 15:00-16:00), sell at the open of the 16:00 UTC bar regardless of price (time exit, fixed clock). STOP-LOSS: one fixed 2.5% below the entry price, the engine''s native intrabar stop (the scout''s original ''closed 1h bar 2.5% below entry'' check is replaced by this intrabar form). At most one trade per day per pair: entry is only possible at the 04:00 open, so this holds by construction. No cooldown needed. All numbers fixed ex ante, no grid: entry window 00:00-04:00 UTC, threshold +1.0%, exit 16:00 UTC, stop 2.5%. Warm-up: 24 bars (longest lookback is 4 bars from the 00:00 open to the 03:00 close; 24 bars guarantee a full UTC day is present; startup_candle_count 24, well under 4500).','2026-11-05T23:01:54.301603+00:00','No price data viewed; only the research context file for H-028 (exploration-split summary numbers of earlier hypotheses) and the validation protocol; BTC, ETH, BNB 1h as available through 2026-11-05 for the developer.','rejected at exploration','Early-UTC-day 1% rally predicts same-day continuation: buy 04:00, sell 16:00 UTC Calibrated exposure: 0.05 (p95 by pair {''BTC/USDT'': 0.09899915214743901, ''ETH/USDT'': 0.12515588019739626, ''BNB/USDT'': 0.15248672787544665}). Calibration trades: {''BTC/USDT'': 357, ''ETH/USDT'': 501, ''BNB/USDT'': 485}.');
INSERT INTO "hypotheses" VALUES('H-029','MondayEffectLong','Closed 1h candles for execution, UTC clock; the trend filter uses CLOSED DAILY candles built from the 1h data (informative 1d merged with merge_informative_pair, forward-filled, so a daily value is visible only after that day has closed). Long only, one position per pair, whole allowed balance, no pyramiding, no take-profit, no sizing hooks, no other filters. FILTER: on the Monday 00:00 UTC bar, the last closed daily candle is Sunday''s; the filter holds when Sunday''s daily close > SMA(50) of daily closes (50 closed daily candles including Sunday). ENTRY: buy at the open of the Monday 00:00 UTC 1h bar (signal evaluated on the closed Sunday daily candle and the 23:00 Sunday bar) if the filter holds and no position is open. If the Monday 00:00 bar or the daily SMA is missing, no trade. EXIT: sell at the open of the Tuesday 00:00 UTC bar (time exit after exactly 24 hourly bars, fixed clock, regardless of price). STOP-LOSS: one fixed 3% below the entry price, the engine''s native intrabar stop (the scout''s closed-bar check is replaced by this intrabar form). At most one trade per week per pair by construction (entry only at the Monday 00:00 open). Cooldown: none needed. All numbers fixed ex ante, no grid: trend mean 50 days, entry Monday 00:00 UTC, hold 24 hours, stop 3%. Warm-up: 1200 bars (50 daily candles = 1200 hourly bars; the SMA is not recursive; startup_candle_count 1200, under the 4500 limit).','2026-11-05T23:19:08.209236+00:00','No price data inspected. Only the research context (hypotheses and exploration summaries of earlier hypotheses for BTC, ETH, BNB 1h) and the Quantpedia page, as of 2026-11-05.','failed: causality checks','Monday-session long in daily uptrend, flat at Tuesday 00:00 UTC');
INSERT INTO "hypotheses" VALUES('H-030','OvernightDropReversal','Closed 1h candles, UTC clock; signals evaluated at bar close, orders executed at the next bar open. Long only, one position per pair, whole allowed balance, no pyramiding, no take-profit, no sizing hooks, no other filters, no cooldown. DEFINITIONS: for each UTC day, O0 = open of the 00:00 UTC bar; C7 = close of the 07:00 UTC bar (the bar covering 07:00-08:00); d = C7 / O0 - 1 (the 8-bar overnight return). DAILY FILTER: build 1d candles from the 1h data (informative 1d via merge_informative_pair, forward-filled, so only completed daily candles are visible); at 08:00 UTC the last closed daily candle is the previous day''s; the filter holds when that previous day''s daily close > SMA(100) of daily closes (100 closed daily candles including that previous day). ENTRY: at the close of the 07:00 UTC bar, if d <= -0.015 AND the daily filter holds AND no position is open, buy at the open of the next bar (the 08:00 UTC bar). If the 00:00 or 07:00 bar or the daily SMA is missing, no signal that day. EXIT: sell at the open of the 16:00 UTC bar of the same day (time exit after 8 hourly bars, fixed clock, regardless of price). STOP-LOSS: one fixed 3% below the entry price, the engine''s native intrabar stop (the scout''s closed-1h-bar check is replaced by this intrabar form). At most one trade per day per pair by construction: entry is only possible at the 08:00 open and the trade is always closed by 16:00. No cooldown needed. All numbers fixed ex ante, no grid: window 00:00-08:00 UTC, drop threshold -1.5%, trend mean 100 days, exit 16:00 UTC, stop 3%. Warm-up: 2500 bars (100 daily candles = 2400 hourly bars for the SMA(100), which is not recursive, plus a partial day and margin; startup_candle_count 2500, under the 4500 limit).','2026-11-05T23:58:43.559204+00:00','No price data seen; only the context file research/context/H-030.md (idea I-013 from the scout, exploration-split summaries of earlier hypotheses) and research/validation-protocol-v2.md. The source page was cited from the scout''s note and was not opened by me.','rejected at exploration','Overnight thin-liquidity drop reversal: buy 08:00 UTC after a 00-08 UTC fall of 1.5% or more in an uptrend Calibrated exposure: 0.1 (p95 by pair {''BTC/USDT'': 0.13128614470588906, ''ETH/USDT'': 0.16457553777213707, ''BNB/USDT'': 0.1825626279763417}). Calibration trades: {''BTC/USDT'': 153, ''ETH/USDT'': 235, ''BNB/USDT'': 260}.');
INSERT INTO "hypotheses" VALUES('H-031','CrossPairCatchUp','Closed 1h candles of BTC/USDT, ETH/USDT and BNB/USDT only (the other two pairs are read as informative 1h pairs, closed bars only, aligned on the same candle timestamp). Long only, spot, one position per traded pair, whole allowed balance. Signal at the close of bar t, order filled at the open of bar t+1. Definitions for traded pair X at bar t: r(t) = close_X(t)/close_X(t-2) - 1. For each of the other two pairs Y, r_Y(t) = close_Y(t)/close_Y(t-2) - 1. L(t) = arithmetic mean of the two r_Y(t). ENTRY at close of bar t when ALL hold: (1) L(t) >= 0.015; (2) r(t) <= L(t) - 0.010; (3) no open position in X; (4) cooldown satisfied. EXIT: time exit after 4 bars held: if the entry fill is at the open of bar e, the exit signal is at the close of bar e+3 and fills at the open of bar e+4 (position held 4 hours). STOP-LOSS: one fixed 1.5% below the entry price, native intrabar stop (triggers as soon as price touches it, not on a close). COOLDOWN: no re-entry for 4 candles after any exit. No take-profit, no pyramiding, no other filters, no trend filter. All numbers fixed ex ante, no grid: 2-bar return length, jump threshold 1.5%, gap 1.0%, hold 4 bars, stop 1.5%, cooldown 4 bars. Warm-up: 50 bars (longest lookback is 2 bars; no recursive indicators; 50 bars covers alignment of the informative pairs).','2026-11-06T00:21:48.601429+00:00','Context file research/context/H-031.md (hypothesis list and exploration-only audit facts); no price data or validation results seen.','rejected at exploration','Cross-pair catch-up: buy the laggard after the other two pairs jump on 1h Calibrated exposure: 0.05 (p95 by pair {''BTC/USDT'': 0.16674868150293887, ''ETH/USDT'': 0.16344308057157353, ''BNB/USDT'': 0.1609015428298164}). Calibration trades: {''BTC/USDT'': 702, ''ETH/USDT'': 575, ''BNB/USDT'': 763}.');
INSERT INTO "hypotheses" VALUES('H-032','VolumeSpikeCrashRebound','Closed 1h candles only; signal evaluated at bar close t, order filled at the open of bar t+1. Long only, spot, one position per pair, whole allowed balance, no pyramiding, no sizing hooks, no other filters. Definitions (completed bars only): r1(t) = close(t)/close(t-1) - 1. S(t) = population-free sample standard deviation (ddof=1) of r1 over the 720 bars ending at t-1 (bars t-720..t-1). V(t) = volume(t) / mean volume of the 168 bars ending at t-1 (bars t-168..t-1). Pos(t) = (close(t)-low(t))/(high(t)-low(t)); if high(t)==low(t) there is no signal. ENTRY at the close of bar t when ALL hold: r1(t) <= -3.0*S(t); r1(t) <= -0.015; V(t) >= 3.0; Pos(t) >= 0.5; no open position; cooldown satisfied; all inputs defined (no NaN). Store the open of the crash bar t as TARGET (fixed at entry). EXIT: at the close of the first bar u >= t+1 (the entry bar is the first one checked) with close(u) >= TARGET, filled at the open of bar u+1; or time exit at the close of bar t+18 (18 bars after the signal bar), filled at the open of bar t+19, whichever comes first. STOP-LOSS: one fixed 4% below the entry price, the engine''s native intrabar stop (replaces the scout''s closed-bar check). COOLDOWN: no re-entry for 6 candles after any exit. No take-profit other than the TARGET exit. All numbers fixed ex ante, no grid: 720-bar volatility window, 3.0 sigma, 1.5% minimum drop, 168-bar volume window, volume multiple 3.0, range position 0.5, time exit 18 bars, stop 4%, cooldown 6. Warm-up: 800 bars (longest lookback is 721 closes for 720 returns; no recursive indicators; startup_candle_count 800, under the 4500 limit).','2026-11-06T09:30:28.082802+00:00','No price data seen; only the context file research/context/H-032.md (tried hypotheses and exploration summaries) and the abstract of the cited paper.','dropped: fewer than 30 trades','Volume-spike hourly crash closing off its low: rebound to crash-bar open DROPPED by the pre-registered rule: calibration trades {''BTC/USDT'': 18, ''ETH/USDT'': 20, ''BNB/USDT'': 13} (< 30 on at least one pair); not retuned.');
INSERT INTO "hypotheses" VALUES('H-033','HourlyShockOverreaction','Closed 1h candles only; signal evaluated at bar close t, order executed at the next bar open (t+1). Long only, one position per pair, whole allowed balance, no pyramiding, no take-profit, no sizing hooks, no other filters. Definition: r4(t) = close(t)/close(t-4) - 1. ENTRY at close of bar t when ALL hold: (1) r4(t) <= -0.04; (2) close(t) > SMA(1200) of close at t (not a long-term downtrend); (3) no open position; (4) cooldown satisfied. Pre-drop price P = close(t-4), stored at signal time. EXIT (signal at a bar close, executed at the next open) when the first of these occurs: (a) close >= P (pre-drop price regained); (b) 24 bars have elapsed since the signal bar t (close of bar t+24, executed at open of t+25). STOP-LOSS: one fixed percentage, 5% below the entry price, as the engine''s native intrabar stop (triggers as soon as price touches it, not on a close). COOLDOWN: no re-entry for 12 candles after any exit. All thresholds fixed in advance and not tuned: shock window 4 bars, shock threshold -4.0%, trend SMA 1200 bars, max hold 24 bars, stop 5%, cooldown 12 bars. Warm-up: 1200 bars (SMA(1200); no recursive indicators; set startup_candle_count to 1200 or slightly more, at most 4500).','2026-11-06T09:46:33.560545+00:00','No price data viewed; only the context file research/context/H-033.md (idea I-016 and tried-hypothesis list, partially read) and research/validation-protocol-v2.md, as of 2026-11-06.','rejected at exploration','Hourly negative-shock overreaction: buy 4h crash close above SMA1200, 24h hold Calibrated exposure: 0.1 (p95 by pair {''BTC/USDT'': 0.10967774312486653, ''ETH/USDT'': 0.18501567310289702, ''BNB/USDT'': 0.1911558714718198}). Calibration trades: {''BTC/USDT'': 99, ''ETH/USDT'': 171, ''BNB/USDT'': 190}.');
INSERT INTO "hypotheses" VALUES('H-034','SessionOpeningRangeBreakout','Closed 1h candles only, UTC clock; signal at bar close, order at next bar open. Long only, one position, whole allowed balance, no pyramiding. OPENING RANGE of each UTC day = the 1h candle opening at 00:00 UTC (covers 00:00-01:00, the same hour the scout''s four 15m bars cover): range high RH = its high, range low RL = its low, height H = RH - RL, midpoint M = (RH + RL)/2. The day is ARMED only if H / RL >= 0.008 (0.8%). ENTRY: on a 1h candle whose open time is between 01:00 and 11:00 UTC inclusive (so its close is at or before 12:00 UTC), if the day is armed, the strategy is flat, no trade has yet been entered that UTC day, and close > RH; order at next open. One trade per day per pair; no re-entry the same day. EXIT at bar close (executed next open), first of: (a) close < M; (b) close >= RH + 1.5 * H (profit target); (c) the candle opening at 19:00 UTC closes (the 20:00 UTC time exit, executed at the 20:00 open). STOP-LOSS: fixed 4% below entry price (native intrabar stop; a safety net wider than the typical half-range midpoint exit, no other stop). Cooldown: none beyond the one-trade-per-day rule. No trend filter, no volume filter, no other filters. Fixed values RH/RL/H/M are frozen from the 00:00 candle and not updated during the day. Positions are never held past 20:00 UTC. The 15m version of the scout (four 15m bars) is replaced by the single 1h candle on the 1h chart as directed; no number is tuned. Warm-up: 48 bars (no indicator; the current day''s 00:00 candle is at most 23 bars back, 48 gives margin).','2026-11-06T10:06:46.254662+00:00','No price data seen; only the exploration-split context file research/context/H-034.md (hypothesis list and cost scenarios) and the validation protocol, as of 2026-11-06.','rejected at exploration','UTC-day opening-range breakout on 1h, wide ranges only, midpoint exit and 20:00 time exit Calibrated exposure: 0.05 (p95 by pair {''BTC/USDT'': 0.1574684987812517, ''ETH/USDT'': 0.16762179657139728, ''BNB/USDT'': 0.18271047756759975}). Calibration trades: {''BTC/USDT'': 761, ''ETH/USDT'': 965, ''BNB/USDT'': 1030}.');
INSERT INTO "hypotheses" VALUES('H-035','HourlyRangeExpansionDrift','Closed 1h candles, UTC; signal evaluated at bar close t, order executed at the open of bar t+1. Long only, one position, whole allowed balance, no pyramiding, no take-profit, no sizing hooks. Definitions: Range(t)=high(t)-low(t). TR(t)=max(high-low, |high-close(t-1)|, |low-close(t-1)|). ATR(t)=simple mean of TR over the 24 bars t-24..t-1 (excluding the current bar). Pos(t)=(close(t)-low(t))/(high(t)-low(t)); if high==low the bar does not qualify. ENTRY at close of bar t when ALL hold: (1) Range(t) >= 3.0*ATR(t); (2) Pos(t) >= 0.8; (3) close(t) > open(t); (4) close(t) > SMA(480) of 1h closes at t; (5) no open position; (6) cooldown satisfied. Buy at the open of t+1. EXIT: (a) signal exit: first bar close (bar u>t) with close(u) < low of the entry-signal bar t, executed at the open of u+1; (b) time exit: 24 bars after entry, executed at that bar''s open (i.e. sell at the open of the 24th bar after the entry bar). STOP-LOSS: fixed 5% below the entry price (native intrabar stop; a catastrophic-loss backstop required by the engine contract, the signal-bar-low exit is the designed exit). COOLDOWN: no re-entry for 6 candles after any exit. No other filters. Warm-up: 500 bars (SMA(480) is the longest lookback; ATR needs 25 bars; no recursive indicators).','2026-11-06T10:29:00.378628+00:00','Context file research/context/H-035.md (exploration-split summaries of earlier hypotheses only); no price data or validation results viewed; idea I-018 text from the scout.','rejected at exploration','Hourly range-expansion bar closing at its high, 24-hour continuation hold in uptrend Calibrated exposure: 0.25 (p95 by pair {''BTC/USDT'': 0.17594119551913687, ''ETH/USDT'': 0.12327484474042484, ''BNB/USDT'': 0.24195534639108884}). Calibration trades: {''BTC/USDT'': 136, ''ETH/USDT'': 123, ''BNB/USDT'': 98}.');
INSERT INTO "hypotheses" VALUES('H-036','USOpenVolumeContinuation','Closed 1h candles only, UTC clock; signal evaluated at bar close, order filled at the next bar open. Long only, spot, one position per pair, whole allowed balance, no pyramiding, no take-profit, no sizing hooks, no other filters. SIGNAL BAR: the 1h bar opening at 14:00 UTC (covers 14:00-15:00). V = its volume. Vref = arithmetic mean of the volume of the 14:00 UTC bars of the previous 20 calendar days (days d-20..d-1, excluding the current day; 480 bars back at most). ENTRY at the close of the 14:00 bar when ALL hold: (1) V >= 2.0 * Vref; (2) close > open; (3) close/open - 1 >= 0.007; (4) close > SMA(200) of 1h closes at that bar; (5) no open position. Buy at the open of the next bar (15:00 UTC). If the 14:00 bar, Vref (fewer than 20 prior 14:00 bars) or the SMA is missing, no signal. EXIT: at the close of the 18:00 UTC bar of the same day (the bar covering 18:00-19:00), sold at the open of the 19:00 bar, i.e. 4 hourly bars held (15,16,17,18), regardless of price. STOP-LOSS: one fixed 1.5% below the entry price, the engine''s native intrabar stop (replaces the scout''s closed-bar check). At most one trade per day per pair by construction (entry only after the 14:00 bar, trade always closed by 19:00). No cooldown needed. All numbers fixed ex ante, no grid: signal hour 14:00 UTC, volume multiple 2.0, reference 20 days, min bar return +0.7%, trend mean 200 bars, hold 4 bars, stop 1.5%. Warm-up: 500 bars (longest lookback is the 14:00 bar 20 days back = 480 bars; SMA(200) is shorter; no recursive indicators; startup_candle_count 500, under the 4500 limit).','2026-11-06T10:53:44.759413+00:00','No price data; only the research context file listing tried hypotheses and exploration summaries (BTC, ETH, BNB 1h), as of 2026-11-06.','rejected at exploration','US-open volume-surge continuation: 14:00 UTC 1h bar, 4-hour hold Calibrated exposure: 0.5 (p95 by pair {''BTC/USDT'': 0.16024009361259794, ''ETH/USDT'': 0.21061864795592833, ''BNB/USDT'': 0.24011482961790173}). Calibration trades: {''BTC/USDT'': 40, ''ETH/USDT'': 57, ''BNB/USDT'': 62}.');
INSERT INTO "hypotheses" VALUES('H-037','MultiTimeframeMACDTrend','Closed candles only; signals evaluated at bar close, orders executed at next bar open. Long only, one position, whole allowed balance, no pyramiding, no take-profit, no sizing hooks. Hourly indicators on 1h closes: MACD line = EMA(12) - EMA(26); signal = EMA(9) of the MACD line (standard recursive EMAs, adjust=False). Daily indicators: build closed UTC daily candles from the 1h data (informative 1d via merge_informative_pair, forward-filled so a daily value is visible only after that day has closed); daily MACD line = EMA(12) - EMA(26) of daily closes, daily signal = EMA(9) of the daily MACD line. DAILY UP at a 1h bar = last closed daily MACD line > last closed daily signal. ENTRY at the close of 1h bar t when: hourly MACD(t) > signal(t) AND hourly MACD(t-1) <= signal(t-1) (cross-up) AND DAILY UP AND no open position; buy at next open. EXIT at the close of bar t (sell at next open) when hourly MACD(t) < signal(t) AND MACD(t-1) >= signal(t-1) (cross-down), OR when DAILY UP becomes false after a daily close (checked on the 1h bar where the new daily value first appears). STOP-LOSS: fixed 5% below entry price (native intrabar stop). No cooldown, no other filters. Warm-up: 4200 bars (175 days: gives the daily EMA26 and the daily signal EMA9 about 7x their span to stabilise; hourly EMAs need far less). startup_candle_count = 4200.','2026-11-06T11:23:09.535008+00:00','No price data viewed; only the research context file (tried hypotheses and exploration summaries through 2026-11-05), the validation protocol, and the Quantpedia page.','failed: causality checks','Hourly MACD cross-up gated by daily MACD uptrend, exit on hourly cross-down');
INSERT INTO "hypotheses" VALUES('H-038','HourlyFailedBreakdownReclaim','Closed 1h candles only; signals at bar close t, order at next bar open. Long only, one position, whole allowed balance, no sizing hooks. DEFINITIONS (bar t = latest closed bar): PL = lowest low of the 480 bars t-483..t-4 (the 480 bars before bar t-3). The bar that set PL must be at index <= t-96 (at least 4 days before t); if the lowest low is tied, use the most recent tied bar. SWEEP: min(low over bars t-3..t) < PL. RECLAIM: close(t) > PL AND (close(t-1) <= PL OR low(t) < PL), i.e. the first close back above PL. ENTRY at close of t when SWEEP and RECLAIM hold, the PL age condition holds, no position is open and the cooldown is satisfied. One entry per sweep (the first reclaim close only). TARGET = highest high of the 24 bars ending at t, fixed at the signal bar. EXIT at the first bar close >= TARGET (executed next open), or at the close of the 48th bar after entry (time stop, executed next open). STOP-LOSS: fixed 3% below entry price (native intrabar stop). This replaces the scout''s ''close below S'' stop with the engine''s fixed percentage stop; S itself is not used. COOLDOWN: no re-entry for 24 candles after any exit. No other filters, no pyramiding. Warm-up: 500 bars (longest lookback 483 bars; no recursive indicators).','2026-11-06T11:46:23.098779+00:00','No price data; only the context file research/context/H-038.md (exploration summaries of earlier hypotheses) and the scout idea I-023.','rejected at exploration','Turtle Soup on 1h: failed 20-day-low sweep reclaimed within 3 bars Calibrated exposure: 0.2 (p95 by pair {''BTC/USDT'': 0.15948409556081067, ''ETH/USDT'': 0.20976678743322874, ''BNB/USDT'': 0.13365580724882023}). Calibration trades: {''BTC/USDT'': 42, ''ETH/USDT'': 54, ''BNB/USDT'': 44}.');
INSERT INTO "hypotheses" VALUES('H-039','WeekendDaytimeSession','Timeframe 1h, UTC clock, closed candles only. Long only, one position per pair, whole allowed balance. DAILY SIGNAL: build the daily candle from 1h data (informative 1d via merge_informative_pair, forward-filled so only the last COMPLETED daily candle is visible). UPTREND(d) is true if the last completed daily close is above the SMA(50) of daily closes (50 completed days, including that day). ENTRY: on Saturday and Sunday only (UTC), when UPTREND is true and no position is open, buy at the open of the 13:00 UTC 1h bar (signal evaluated on the close of the 12:00 UTC bar, so the order fills at the 13:00 open). One entry per calendar day at most; if the 12:00 or 13:00 bar is missing, skip that day. EXIT: sell at the open of the 21:00 UTC bar (signal at the close of the 20:00 UTC bar), i.e. a holding period of 8 hourly bars (13:00-21:00). Also force the exit if the position is still open at that time for any reason; never hold overnight. STOP-LOSS: fixed 3% below the entry price, native intrabar stop (triggers as soon as price touches it). No take-profit, no pyramiding, no other filters, no cooldown (the entry is at most once per day by construction). Weekday definition: day-of-week of the candle open time in UTC, Saturday=5, Sunday=6. Expected trades: about 104 weekend days per year, UPTREND true on roughly half to two thirds, so about 50-70 trades per year per pair. Warm-up: 1300 bars (SMA(50) of daily closes = 1200 hourly bars plus 100 bars margin for day alignment and the merge).','2026-11-06T12:11:26.541506+00:00','No price data seen; only the context file research/context/H-039.md (exploration summaries of earlier hypotheses) and research/validation-protocol-v2.md, as of 2026-11-06. BTC, ETH, BNB 1h/1d candles were not inspected.','rejected at exploration','Weekend US-daytime session long (Sat/Sun 13:00-21:00 UTC) in a 50-day daily uptrend Calibrated exposure: 0.15 (p95 by pair {''BTC/USDT'': 0.17485390325020234, ''ETH/USDT'': 0.16010904597536457, ''BNB/USDT'': 0.23332921320288014}). Calibration trades: {''BTC/USDT'': 365, ''ETH/USDT'': 367, ''BNB/USDT'': 368}.');
INSERT INTO "hypotheses" VALUES('H-040','DailyNR7Breakout','Closed candles only; strategy runs on 1h. Daily candles are built from completed UTC days (informative 1d via merge_informative_pair, only closed days used). Long only, one position, whole allowed balance, no pyramiding, no take-profit. DEFINITIONS: for UTC day D, range(D) = high(D) - low(D). Day D is NR7 when range(D) is strictly smaller than range of each of the 6 days D-1..D-6. SMA50d = simple mean of the last 50 closed daily closes. SIGNAL DAY = the UTC day after an NR7 day D (day D+1); only the most recent closed day D = yesterday is considered, so no entries on any other day. ENTRY: on signal day, if the last closed daily close (close of D) > SMA50d computed at D, then at the first 1h bar t of the signal day whose close > high(D) AND whose close time is at or before 20:00 UTC (i.e. bar open hour <= 19:00 UTC), signal at the close of bar t and order executed at the next 1h open. At most one entry per NR7 day; if no qualifying bar occurs, nothing is entered that day. If a position is already open, the signal is ignored. EXIT (evaluated at 1h bar close, executed at next open), whichever first: (a) 1h close < low(D) of the NR7 day that triggered the entry; (b) 48 1h bars elapsed since entry (time exit). STOP-LOSS: one fixed native intrabar stop at 3% below entry price (a catastrophic-loss cap; the NR7-low exit in (a) is the normal exit and is checked on closed bars as an exit signal, not as a stop). COOLDOWN: none beyond the one-entry-per-NR7-day rule. No other filters. Fixed parameters: NR window 7 days, SMA 50 days, entry cutoff 20:00 UTC, time exit 48 bars, stop 3%. Exposure: fixed share of the account chosen by the lab rule (largest 5% grid value with block-bootstrap p95 closed-trade drawdown <= 25% on all pairs, from this rule''s own exploration trades at base cost and full exposure; fewer than 30 trades on a pair drops the hypothesis, no retuning). Warm-up: 1500 bars (50 daily closes = 1200 1h bars plus the 7-day NR window and margin for the incomplete first day).','2026-11-06T12:35:12.686740+00:00','No price data seen; only the context file research/context/H-040.md (tried-hypothesis list, exploration summaries for other families) and the idea I-022 text. Intended data: BTC, ETH, BNB 1h through the exploration split.','not approved at validation','Daily NR7 compression day, next-day upside breakout entered on 1h in a 50-day uptrend Calibrated exposure: 0.35 (p95 by pair {''BTC/USDT'': 0.14513556160277166, ''ETH/USDT'': 0.12667573855511524, ''BNB/USDT'': 0.24240659460074057}). Calibration trades: {''BTC/USDT'': 95, ''ETH/USDT'': 80, ''BNB/USDT'': 87}.');
INSERT INTO "hypotheses" VALUES('H-041','WeeklyAnchoredVWAPReclaim','Closed 1h candles, UTC; signals at bar close, order at next bar open; long only, one position, whole allowed balance. Weekly VWAP(t) = sum(typical*volume)/sum(volume) over all 1h bars from Monday 00:00 UTC through bar t inclusive, typical=(high+low+close)/3; it re-anchors (resets) every Monday 00:00 UTC. dev(t)=close(t)/VWAP(t)-1. A bar is ELIGIBLE if its open time is Monday 11:00 UTC or later in the same week (at least 12 bars of the week completed, i.e. 12 bars including the signal bar). BELOW-RUN: consecutive bars with close < VWAP, all inside the current week. SETUP: the BELOW-RUN that ended at bar t-1 has length >= 8 bars AND min dev over that run <= -0.010 (lowest close at least 1.0% below the VWAP of its own bar). ENTRY at close of bar t when: ELIGIBLE, close(t) > VWAP(t) (first close above VWAP after the run, so close(t-1) < VWAP(t-1)), the SETUP holds, close(t) > SMA(480) of 1h closes at t, bar t is not the Sunday 23:00 bar, and no open position. EXIT at close of bar t (executed next open) on the first of: (a) close(t) < VWAP(t)*(1-0.007); (b) bar t is the Sunday 23:00 UTC bar (week end); (c) 48 bars have elapsed since the entry bar. STOP-LOSS: fixed 3% below entry price (native intrabar stop). COOLDOWN: none (0 candles); a new entry needs a fresh SETUP. No take-profit, no pyramiding, no other filters. Warm-up: 500 bars (SMA(480) plus margin; VWAP is non-recursive and needs only the current week, at most 168 bars).','2026-11-06T13:31:29.138879+00:00','No price data seen; only the research context file for H-041 (exploration-split summaries of earlier hypotheses) and the validation protocol.','rejected at exploration','Weekly Monday-anchored VWAP reclaim after a sustained dip, in an SMA(480) uptrend Calibrated exposure: 0.1 (p95 by pair {''BTC/USDT'': 0.1202444313119522, ''ETH/USDT'': 0.08921277301058608, ''BNB/USDT'': 0.18171919203567055}). Calibration trades: {''BTC/USDT'': 210, ''ETH/USDT'': 236, ''BNB/USDT'': 252}.');
INSERT INTO "ideas" VALUES('I-001','S20261104T205946Z','Daily RSI(2) oversold dip buy in 200-day uptrend, exit above 5-day SMA','blog','https://therighttrader.com/learn/trading-strategies/rsi-2-strategy','RSI 2 Strategy (therighttrader.com)','unknown','Signals from closed DAILY candles built from the 1h data, executed at the next 1h open. RSI(2) uses Wilder smoothing on daily closes. ENTRY: daily close > SMA(200 days) of daily close AND RSI(2) < 10 AND no open position. EXIT: first daily close above SMA(5 days) of daily close, OR daily close below SMA(200 days). No profit target, no pyramiding. Optional protective stop (not part of the published exit): none in the base rule; a developer may add a fixed percentage stop below entry. Free numbers: RSI length 2, threshold 10, exit average 5, trend average 200.','Very short-term sell-offs inside an established uptrend are often forced or impatient selling (liquidations, panic sellers) that overshoots; liquidity takers pay a concession to dip buyers, and price snaps back toward its short mean. The source gives only a brief rationale (extreme readings flag dips; the 200-day filter avoids downtrends); the liquidity-overshoot story is the closest honest mechanism.','1d',200,4,1,9.0,'DailyRSI2Dip','89cdd0d318c9fa83fc961babbf54823dd6a77b3395b6d4a6aca0d21b74512381','registered','formalised as H-019',2.9379,'H-019','2026-11-04T21:00:41.983635+00:00');
INSERT INTO "ideas" VALUES('I-002','S20261105T154404Z','Daily Double 7: buy a 7-day closing low above the 200-day mean, sell a 7-day closing high','blog','https://strategyquant.com/blog/larry-connors-double-7-strategy-tested-on-spy-and-8-other-markets/','Larry Connors'' Double 7 Strategy: Tested on SPY and 8 Other Markets','unknown','Daily signals from closed daily candles built from the 1h data; orders executed at the next 1h open. Long only, one position per pair, whole balance. ENTRY when a daily close is above the 200-day simple moving average of daily closes AND that close is less than or equal to the lowest daily close of the last 7 days (including the current day) AND no position is open. EXIT when a daily close is greater than or equal to the highest daily close of the last 7 days (including the current day). No stop, no profit target, no time exit. Lookbacks: 7 days for entry channel, 7 days for exit channel, 200 days for the trend filter.','Counterparty: short-horizon sellers who capitulate or de-risk after a few down days inside a long-term uptrend, pushing price below fair value for a short time; liquidity-demanding panic sellers pay a premium to exit. Short-term reversal after a pullback is paid to the buyer who supplies liquidity. The source gives no mechanism beyond the stock-index mean reversion observation; this is the closest honest one.','1d',200,3,1,9.0,'Double7ChannelDip','f0f19b8980a768896d77b527e47b9400160e7b68404b216f53ba76ccf5891bcf','registered','formalised as H-020',3.3251,'H-020','2026-11-05T15:44:47.191227+00:00');
INSERT INTO "ideas" VALUES('I-003','S20261105T172127Z','Daily internal bar strength dip buy in 200-day uptrend','repo','https://doc.stocksharp.com/en/api-examples/0927_Internal_Bar_Strength_IBS','Internal Bar Strength IBS Strategy (StockSharp docs)','unknown','Daily signals from closed UTC daily candles built from 1h data, executed at the next 1h open. IBS = (close - low) / (high - low) of the daily candle; skip days with zero range. ENTRY when a daily candle closes with IBS < 0.2 AND daily close > SMA(200 days) AND no open position. EXIT when a later daily candle closes with IBS >= 0.8. Safety exit: daily close below the 200-day SMA. Optional hard stop 12% below entry. Long only, one position per pair, whole balance. The source uses 0.2 and 0.8 thresholds on 4h bars with no trend filter; the 200-day filter and daily frame are my adaptation.','A close near the day''s low in an uptrend often reflects forced selling or liquidity-driven pressure at the end of the day. Dip buyers who provide liquidity are paid when price reverts the next sessions. The source gives no mechanism; this is the usual short-term reversal / liquidity-provision explanation.','1d',200,4,1,14.0,'DailyIBSDip','665ca9337a26f817ae3886f1d35a3643611d21f22d9a804bd196a0b8eec4e1be','registered','formalised as H-021',3.1905,'H-021','2026-11-05T17:22:20.894055+00:00');
INSERT INTO "ideas" VALUES('I-004','S20261105T172127Z','Connors 3-day lower highs and lows pullback in 200-day uptrend','blog','https://www.tradingview.com/script/2DMs2jT9','Larry Connors 3-day high/low method (TradingView open-source script)','unknown','Daily signals from closed UTC daily candles built from 1h data, executed at the next 1h open. ENTRY when a daily candle closes with: close > SMA(200 days); close < SMA(5 days); and three consecutive days of falling range, meaning each of the last three daily candles has both a lower high and a lower low than the candle before it (today vs yesterday, yesterday vs two days ago, two days ago vs three days ago); and no open position. EXIT when a daily close is above SMA(5 days). Safety exit: daily close below SMA(200 days) or 12% below entry. Long only, one position per pair, whole balance, no add-ons (the source''s optional add-on is excluded).','Three successive days of lower highs and lows inside a long-term uptrend is a short-lived selling streak. Impatient sellers and stop-triggered holders push price below its short mean, and buyers who provide liquidity are paid when price snaps back to the 5-day mean. The source states no mechanism; this is the standard short-term reversal explanation.','1d',200,4,1,8.0,'ThreeDayLowerRangeDip','57b1f8d970a707f77122887507d9d8c89b89aa3f4c65bdc7c1faea6abfa43a1f','registered','formalised as H-022',2.5137,'H-022','2026-11-05T17:22:20.900770+00:00');
INSERT INTO "ideas" VALUES('I-005','S20261105T183908Z','Daily R3: three falling RSI(2) readings ending below 10, in 200-day uptrend','repo','https://in.tradingview.com/script/5CDSns2I-R3-ETF-Strategy','R3 ETF Strategy (TradingView open-source script, after Connors and Alvarez)','unknown','All signals from closed daily candles (UTC) built from 1h data, executed at next 1h open. Compute RSI(2) on daily closes and SMA(200 days) of daily close. ENTRY when a daily candle closes with: close > SMA200 AND RSI(2) has fallen on each of the last three days (RSI today < RSI yesterday < RSI two days ago < RSI three days ago) AND RSI(2) three days ago was below 60 AND RSI(2) today is below 10, with no open position. EXIT when a daily close has RSI(2) above 70. No stop, no profit target. One position per pair, whole balance.','A multi-day one-way slide that ends in extreme short-term oversold inside a long-term uptrend is typically forced or panicked selling (liquidations, stop runs). Liquidity providers and dip buyers on the other side collect the usual partial snap-back. The source gives no mechanism beyond the ETF mean-reversion claim; this is the closest honest one.','1d',200,5,1,7.0,'DailyR3Streak','ab7bf7d7a72fee656de5e0d908a5b8774dca7b80618d1c014fb646352f63974c','registered','formalised as H-023',2.2501,'H-023','2026-11-05T18:39:53.248450+00:00');
INSERT INTO "ideas" VALUES('I-006','S20261105T191024Z','Late-evening UTC two-hour window long in daily uptrend and high-volatility regime','blog','https://quantpedia.com/the-seasonality-of-bitcoin/','The Seasonality of Bitcoin (Quantpedia)','none','Hourly candles, UTC. Regime is read from daily data at 00:00 UTC and holds for that whole UTC day. Uptrend: the last closed daily close is above the 50-day SMA of daily closes. High volatility: the 30-day standard deviation of hourly returns is above the median of that same measure over the previous 180 days (shortened from the source''s 365 to fit the lab''s lookback limit). ENTRY: on days when both hold, buy at the open of the 21:00 UTC hourly candle. EXIT: sell at the open of the 23:00 UTC candle (two hour hold, no stop). One position, whole balance, no other filters.','The source offers no firm mechanism. The closest honest story: liquidity thins and US-evening order flow, plus retail and derivative-hedging flows near the daily roll, push prices up late in the UTC day; they pay for immediacy. The effect is likely strongest when volatility is high and the trend is up. Academic work finds time-of-day effects unstable across periods, and a 2-hour hold may not clear 0.35% costs.','1h',4320,4,1,120.0,'IntradayUTCWindow','32c57879124fbc9ba3d87a70c4043fc0a304753b05369faa13300a0749af269f','dropped','forbidden by the lab: derivatives',NULL,NULL,'2026-11-05T19:11:12.743800+00:00');
INSERT INTO "ideas" VALUES('I-007','S20261105T191114Z','Daily lottery-jump (MAX) persistence gate with 20-day mean exit','paper','https://research.birmingham.ac.uk/en/publications/max-momentum-in-cryptocurrency-markets/','MAX momentum in cryptocurrency markets','none','Daily signals from closed UTC daily candles, executed at next 1h open. MAX(t) = largest daily close-to-close return among the last 30 daily closes including the just-closed day. Jump-regime is on when MAX(t) is at or above the median of MAX over the previous 150 days (excluding today). ENTRY: jump-regime on AND daily close > SMA(50 days) AND daily close > highest daily close of the prior 10 days AND no open position. EXIT: daily close < SMA(20 days). Hard stop 12% below entry, checked on closed bars. No re-entry for 3 days after exit. Long only, one position, whole balance. Single-asset time-series adaptation of the cross-sectional MAX momentum finding (the paper sorts coins; this is my own adaptation).','The source says crypto has lottery-like, positively skewed payoffs and that coins with large recent maximum daily returns keep earning higher returns (attention and speculative demand persist). The other side is late sellers and contrarians who treat a spike as an overreaction and sell into continuing attention-driven demand. The source gives no single-asset version; this is the closest honest reading.','1d',180,6,0,7.0,'DailyMaxJumpMomentum','26d6ec0a3d544ee41d461c309ade4f0676306baf5b0da78dbf251d86adb11fc9','registered','formalised as H-024',1.9705,'H-024','2026-11-05T19:12:04.019476+00:00');
INSERT INTO "ideas" VALUES('I-008','S20261105T193815Z','Daily nearness-to-26-week-high momentum gate with hysteresis exit','paper','https://wp.ffu.vse.cz/artkey/wps-202301-0003_impact-of-size-and-volume-on-cryptocurrency-momentum-and-reversal.php','Impact of size and volume on cryptocurrency momentum and reversal (FFA Working Papers)','unknown','Daily signals from closed daily candles, executed at the next 1h open. Define H(d) = highest daily high of the 182 days ending at day d (including d). Nearness N(d) = close(d)/H(d). ENTRY when a daily candle closes with N(d) >= 0.95 and no position is open. EXIT when a daily candle closes with N(d) < 0.85. Between 0.85 and 0.95 hold the current state (hysteresis). No other filters, no take-profit, no leverage, one position per pair. Parameters: window 182 days, entry 0.95, exit 0.85.','Investors anchor on recent highs and are reluctant to bid prices up to and through them, so good news is underreacted to near the high (George-Hwang anchoring). Sellers who sell near the high give away the slow drift. The paper gives distance from the k-week high as a predictor for large liquid coins, which BTC, ETH and BNB are; the exact trading rule here is my own adaptation.','1d',182,3,0,6.0,'NearHighAnchorGate','e5a3bef73e8f4111682b78c32bd30b6f2c625add057bfa8a7203a9db45368706','registered','formalised as H-026',2.3001,'H-026','2026-11-05T19:39:11.958565+00:00');
INSERT INTO "ideas" VALUES('I-009','S20261105T193815Z','Daily Keltner upper-band close breakout in uptrend, exit at EMA20','repo','https://doc.stocksharp.com/en/api-examples/0955_Keltner_Channel','Keltner Channel Strategy (StockSharp API examples)','unknown','Daily signals from closed daily candles, executed at the next 1h open. Keltner mid = EMA(20) of daily close; ATR(20) simple/Wilder average of daily true range; upper band = mid + 1.5*ATR(20). ENTRY when a daily close is above the upper band, the previous daily close was at or below the previous upper band (fresh cross), daily close > SMA(100), and no position is open. EXIT when a daily close falls below EMA(20), or close is 2.0*ATR(20) (at entry) below the entry price (stop checked on daily closes). Source uses 1.5 band multiplier and 20-length; I adapted the lower-band reversion idea into a trend breakout on the upside, so the rule is my own.','A close beyond 1.5 ATR above the 20-day mean marks a volatility expansion; slower participants and stop-driven sellers/short covers chase it over following days, so the move tends to continue until price falls back to the mean. Source gives no mechanism for the breakout direction; this is the closest honest one.','1d',100,5,1,8.0,'DailyKeltnerBreakout','cccd11193f5e4e567ef17ac9e808e506c771be7bbd02d52d0f77d0938103ead2','registered','formalised as H-025',2.7201,'H-025','2026-11-05T19:39:11.965980+00:00');
INSERT INTO "ideas" VALUES('I-010','S20261105T202520Z','Daily Supertrend (ATR 10, x3) long-only flip trend follower','repo','https://stocksharp.com/store/strategies.0010_super_trend/','Super Trend (C#) - StockSharp strategy store','unknown','Daily signals from closed daily candles built from the 1h data, executed at the next 1h open. Compute ATR(10) on daily candles (Wilder smoothing). Basic bands: hl2 +/- 3.0 * ATR. Final lower band only ratchets up while the close stays above it and resets when price closes below it; the Supertrend line is the final lower band in an uptrend and the final upper band in a downtrend. ENTRY: the daily close crosses from below to above the Supertrend line (trend flips to up) and no position is open. EXIT: the daily close crosses below the Supertrend line (trend flips to down); the line itself acts as a trailing stop. No other filters, no take-profit, no fixed stop. Long only, whole balance, one position per pair.','Trend followers who trade a volatility-scaled trailing stop profit from slow information diffusion and herding in crypto: large moves tend to continue, while the ATR-scaled trail cuts losers. The other side is late mean-reversion sellers and traders who fade breakouts. The source gives no mechanism beyond the technical description, so this is the closest honest one.','1d',60,2,1,7.0,'DailySupertrendFlip','3034b0e2ca74659971519f5b023859a531eef36ea6ab6d85dac6a37a8605ba0f','registered','formalised as H-027',2.9843,'H-027','2026-11-05T20:26:17.530457+00:00');
INSERT INTO "ideas" VALUES('I-011','S20261105T225949Z','Intraday momentum: strong early-UTC-day move predicts late-day continuation','paper','https://research.birmingham.ac.uk/en/publications/bitcoin-intraday-time-series-momentum/','Bitcoin intraday time series momentum','unknown','Hourly candles, UTC clock. At the close of the 03:00 UTC bar (the bar covering 03:00-04:00), compute r = that close / open of the 00:00 UTC bar of the same day - 1. If r >= +1.0% and no position is open, buy at the open of the next bar (04:00 UTC). Exit at the close of the 15:00 UTC bar (executed at the 16:00 open) regardless of price. Stop: exit if a closed 1h bar is 2.5% below entry. At most one trade per day per pair. No other filters. All signals hourly.','The source reports that the early-session return positively predicts a later-session return and attributes it to liquidity provision (dealers laying off inventory gradually), not late news. The other side is those who sell into the early move too cheaply and must re-buy later. The source defines sessions by volume, not UTC clock, so fixed UTC windows are an adaptation. The gross move after a >=1% early move must exceed 0.35% to pay; this is not guaranteed.','1h',5,5,0,40.0,'IntradayEarlySessionMomentum','82f6d343e7210d1c657bf042cd0bc1e35d194a13a08ee40455ed704391044fe1','registered','formalised as H-028',2.7647,'H-028','2026-11-05T23:01:23.137342+00:00');
INSERT INTO "ideas" VALUES('I-012','S20261105T225949Z','Monday-session long in daily uptrend, flat by Monday close','blog','https://quantpedia.com/are-there-any-simple-calendar-effects-in-bitcoin-market/','Are There Any Simple Calendar Effects in Bitcoin Market?','unknown','Signals from closed daily candles plus the hourly clock. Condition: the last closed daily close is above its 50-day SMA of daily closes. Entry: buy at the 00:00 UTC bar open on Monday if the condition holds and no position is open. Exit: sell at the open of the Tuesday 00:00 UTC bar (i.e. hold exactly 24 hours), or earlier on a close-based stop when a closed 1h bar is 3% below entry. One trade per week per pair. Daily filter is daily; entry and exit are on the hourly chart.','The source documents a higher Monday return and lower weekend volume in Bitcoin, likening it to currency markets, and suggests retail dominance causes inefficiency. It also found the effect inconsistent over time and concludes there is no reliable exploitable pattern. Closest honest mechanism: weekend thin liquidity lets sellers push price down and Monday''s return of institutional flow restores it. A 24h Monday move must exceed 0.35% to pay, which is doubtful; this is a low-confidence diversifier.','1h',1200,4,0,35.0,'MondayEffectLong','29a7320f6352081aa6b1be72d265119cc87dc73411ae768f29af67a5f4f48398','registered','formalised as H-029',2.2742,'H-029','2026-11-05T23:01:23.141965+00:00');
INSERT INTO "ideas" VALUES('I-013','S20261105T225949Z','Thin-liquidity overnight drop reversal: buy 08:00 UTC after sharp 00-08 UTC fall','blog','https://quantpedia.com/are-there-any-simple-calendar-effects-in-bitcoin-market/','Are There Any Simple Calendar Effects in Bitcoin Market?','unknown','Hourly candles, UTC clock. At the close of the 07:00-08:00 UTC bar compute d = close/open(00:00 UTC bar of the same day) - 1 (the overnight return over 8 bars). If d <= -1.5% and the last closed daily close is above the 100-day SMA of daily closes and no position is open, buy at the next bar open. Exit at the open of the 16:00 UTC bar the same day (when US hours are active), or earlier if a closed 1h bar is 3% below entry. One trade per day per pair. Daily trend filter is daily; others hourly.','The source notes volume is lowest overnight and higher while US markets are open. Moves made in thin hours are less backed by real flow, so sellers who pushed price down through an empty book may be partly reversed when liquidity returns. This mechanism is the closest honest one, not stated by the source. The 0.35% round-trip cost needs a rebound well above that after a 1.5% drop, which fits only if reversals are sizeable. This is the opposite sign of idea 1, so it is a distinct test.','1h',2400,5,0,25.0,'OvernightDropReversal','768a26ce45c88544d9c469feda4abfe9b762d981308a5aab5408e14b53ebfc08','registered','formalised as H-030',2.1333,'H-030','2026-11-05T23:01:23.146453+00:00');
INSERT INTO "ideas" VALUES('I-014','S20261106T002034Z','UTC-day opening-range breakout on 15m, wide ranges only, midpoint stop and time exit','blog','https://www.altrady.com/blog/crypto-trading-strategies/orb-trading-strategy','ORB Trading Strategy (Altrady)','unknown','15m closed candles, UTC clock; signal at bar close, order at next bar open. Each UTC day, the opening range is the highest high and lowest low of the four 15m bars from 00:00 to 01:00 UTC. The day is armed only if (range high - range low)/range low >= 0.8%. ENTRY: between 01:00 and 12:00 UTC, the first 15m close above the range high, if flat and no trade yet today (one trade per day per pair). EXIT, first of: 15m close below the range midpoint; 15m close >= range high + 1.5 x range height (profit target); 20:00 UTC bar close (time exit). No re-entry the same day. No trend filter.','Overnight/early-session range compression is followed by a directional move when the first participants of the Asian-to-Europe handover (stops, breakout buyers, momentum chasers) hit the book; late sellers who fade the range are forced to cover or chase. The width filter keeps the range at 0.8% or more, so a 1.5x range-height target is a move well above the 0.35% round-trip cost; the midpoint stop caps the loss at about half a range. Source gives the generic ORB rule and no crypto mechanism; this is the closest honest one.','15m',4,5,0,90.0,'SessionOpeningRangeBreakout','09c197ba5057f885ffac40f9c143bbe0e6ff07497c00a7435c0227ff0818cfb3','registered','formalised as H-034',2.2442,'H-034','2026-11-06T00:21:23.846236+00:00');
INSERT INTO "ideas" VALUES('I-015','S20261106T002034Z','Cross-pair catch-up: buy the laggard after the other two pairs jump on 1h','paper','https://irep.iium.edu.my/73405/','Lead-lag relationship between Bitcoin and Ethereum: evidence from hourly and daily data','unknown','1h closed candles of the three pairs; signal at bar close, order at next bar open. For pair X at bar t, let L(t) = mean of the 2-bar returns (close(t)/close(t-2) - 1) of the other two pairs, and r(t) = X''s own 2-bar return. ENTRY when L(t) >= 1.5%, r(t) <= L(t) - 1.0% (X has not followed), and no position in X. EXIT at the close of the 4th bar after entry (time exit), or earlier if X closes below its entry price by 1.5% (stop checked on closed bars). Cooldown 4 bars after exit. No other filters.','Price discovery is not instant across pairs: the source finds causality running between BTC and ETH on hourly data (mixed, and it warns that profit is hard). Smaller or less liquid pairs absorb a large move in the others with a delay because market makers and arbitrageurs re-quote them in steps, so the laggard catches up. Only large jumps (1.5% or more with a gap of 1% or more) are used, so that a catch-up of a fraction of the gap can exceed the 0.35% cost. The source gives no tradable rule; the edge is doubtful and is left for the gates to judge.','1h',2,5,0,25.0,'CrossPairCatchUp','d9766f4169b7f060f3429359bcb13c51cb28245e0aa47dbef544a532be4171e5','registered','formalised as H-031',2.8095,'H-031','2026-11-06T00:21:23.854941+00:00');
INSERT INTO "ideas" VALUES('I-016','S20261106T092700Z','Hourly negative-shock overreaction: buy 4h crash close, 24h hold','paper','https://ideas.repec.org/a/taf/recsxx/v25y2022i1p1294-1313.html','Intraday Bitcoin price shocks: when bad news is good news','unknown','Closed 1h candles only; signal at bar close, order at next bar open. Long only, one position per pair, whole balance. r4(t) = close(t)/close(t-4) - 1. ENTRY at close of bar t when r4(t) <= -4.0% AND close(t) > SMA(1200 bars) of close (not a long-term downtrend) AND no open position. EXIT at the close of bar t+24 (executed next open), or earlier at close if close >= close(t-4) (the pre-drop price); hard stop: close 5% below entry price, checked on closed bars. No re-entry within 12 bars of an exit. All thresholds are fixed in advance, not tuned.','Forced sellers (liquidations, stop cascades, panic market orders) push price below fair value within hours; liquidity providers and patient buyers are paid to absorb the flow as price relaxes back over 6-24 hours. The cited paper reports overreaction after negative hourly shocks that grows over 6-24 hours; it gives no explicit rule, so thresholds here are my own. A 4% drop with partial recovery to the pre-drop price targets a move well above the 0.35% cost.','1h',1200,5,1,12.0,'HourlyShockOverreaction','7f6565fe76bbcacb50b420c8f0d88a0de60a9ef0cec4428a7a715efba7807e7c','registered','formalised as H-033',3.7179,'H-033','2026-11-06T09:29:52.111753+00:00');
INSERT INTO "ideas" VALUES('I-017','S20261106T092700Z','Volatility-scaled hourly crash with volume spike, rebound to crash-bar open','paper','https://ideas.repec.org/a/taf/recsxx/v25y2022i1p1294-1313.html','Intraday Bitcoin price shocks: when bad news is good news','unknown','Closed 1h candles only; signal at bar close, order at next bar open. Long only, one position per pair, whole balance. r1(t) = close(t)/close(t-1) - 1. S(t) = standard deviation of r1 over the 720 bars ending at t-1. V(t) = volume(t) divided by the mean volume of the 168 bars ending at t-1. ENTRY at close of bar t when r1(t) <= -3.0*S(t) AND r1(t) <= -1.5% AND V(t) >= 3 AND (close(t)-low(t))/(high(t)-low(t)) >= 0.5 (bar closes in its upper half, rejecting the low) AND no open position. EXIT at the close of the first bar with close >= open of the crash bar t (executed next open), or at the close of bar t+18, whichever is first. Stop: close 4% below entry on closed bars. Cooldown 6 bars after exit.','A volume-spiking crash bar that closes off its low shows forced or panic selling being absorbed; the cited paper finds overreaction after negative hourly shocks that keeps reversing for 6-24 hours. Sellers who dumped at the low pay the rebound to patient buyers. The paper gives no explicit rule; the volume spike and range-position confirmation are my own additions. The target (crash-bar open) is at least 1.5% above the signal close, above the 0.35% cost.','1h',720,6,1,15.0,'VolumeSpikeCrashRebound','1a0cac8402259fbca65a082c11d117296894ee7373c0d3fb20d31d7c1734c3f1','registered','formalised as H-032',3.7568,'H-032','2026-11-06T09:29:52.120194+00:00');
INSERT INTO "ideas" VALUES('I-018','S20261106T102744Z','Hourly range-expansion bar closing at its high, continuation hold in uptrend','blog','https://www.altrady.com/blog/crypto-trading-strategies/orb-trading-strategy','Opening range breakout (ORB) trading strategy - Altrady','unknown','Closed 1h candles, UTC. Range(t)=high-low of bar t; ATR(t)=mean true range of the 24 bars before t. Pos(t)=(close-low)/(high-low). ENTRY at close of bar t when ALL hold: Range(t) >= 3.0*ATR(t); Pos(t) >= 0.8; close(t) > open(t); close(t) > SMA(480) of 1h closes; no open position. Buy at next bar open. EXIT at the first of: a bar close below the low of the entry-signal bar (stop, executed next open); or 24 bars after entry (time exit at that bar''s open). No re-entry for 6 bars after an exit. No pyramiding, no take-profit.','The source only suggests taking breakouts whose candle is large versus recent candles and closes near its extreme; it gives no mechanism. Closest honest one: an abnormally large bar closing at its high marks forced or stop-driven buying (short covering, breakout stops) that clears liquidity; slower participants and algos chase over the following hours, so drift continues. A 3x-ATR shock bar makes a mean gross move above 0.35% plausible.','1h',480,6,0,40.0,'HourlyRangeExpansionDrift','3838cff88335c796f414b597ad4caab313c2ce75a6ecf042c7e40f9cddd542f2','registered','formalised as H-035',2.2692,'H-035','2026-11-06T10:28:34.973008+00:00');
INSERT INTO "ideas" VALUES('I-019','S20261106T105207Z','US-session volume-surge continuation: 1h bar at US open, 4-hour hold','blog','https://quantpedia.com/Blog/Details/are-there-any-simple-calendar-effects-in-bitcoin-market','Are There Any Simple Calendar Effects in Bitcoin Market?','none','Closed 1h candles, UTC clock. Signal bar is the 1h bar opening at 14:00 UTC (covers 14:00-15:00, just after the US cash open). Let V = its volume and Vref = mean volume of the 14:00 bars of the previous 20 days. ENTRY at the close of that bar if V >= 2.0 * Vref AND close > open AND (close/open - 1) >= 0.007 AND close > SMA(200 bars) of 1h closes AND no open position; buy at the next bar open (15:00). EXIT at the close of the 18:00 bar (executed at next open, i.e. 4 bars held), or earlier if a closed bar is more than 1.5% below the entry price. At most one trade per day per pair. No other filters.','Bitcoin activity is highest while US markets are open and thin overnight. A volume-confirmed up move at the US open is likely information-driven flow from institutional and ETF-linked participants who execute in slices over several hours, so price keeps drifting as the remaining orders arrive. The other side is slower liquidity providers and sellers who anchor on the pre-open price. The source describes only the time-of-day volume pattern, not a rule; the rule is my own construction. Whether the continuation exceeds the 0.35% cost is uncertain, which is why the filter demands a large volume and price shock.','1h',480,6,0,40.0,'USOpenVolumeContinuation','9d7cd866ab7fe3e1b0e18515ce1e35fc46e82c0cef21ef108f2bfc238a5db84d','registered','formalised as H-036',2.1667,'H-036','2026-11-06T10:53:14.326360+00:00');
INSERT INTO "ideas" VALUES('I-020','S20261106T105207Z','Weekend thin-liquidity drop reversal: buy Sunday-morning dip, exit Sunday close','blog','https://quantpedia.com/Blog/Details/are-there-any-simple-calendar-effects-in-bitcoin-market','Are There Any Simple Calendar Effects in Bitcoin Market?','none','Closed 1h candles, UTC clock, Saturday and Sunday only. Define D = close of the current bar / highest close of the prior 24 bars - 1. ENTRY at the close of any bar whose open time is Saturday 00:00 UTC through Sunday 15:00 UTC when D <= -0.03 (price at least 3% below its 24-hour high close), the bar''s close is above its open (first green bar after the drop), close > SMA(1200 bars) of 1h closes, and no position is open; buy at the next bar open. EXIT when close >= the highest close of the prior 24 bars measured at entry signal time minus half the drop (i.e. half the drop recovered), or at the close of the Sunday 23:00 UTC bar, or on a closed bar 2.5% below entry. One position per pair, at most one trade per weekend per pair.','Weekend volume is lower, so order books are thinner and forced sellers (stop cascades, liquidations of leveraged holders felt on spot) move price further than information justifies. Market makers widen spreads and refill depth only slowly; the buyers who step in when depth returns collect the recovery. The source documents lower weekend volume but no rule, so this is my own construction. A 3% drop with half recovered gives a gross target near 1.5%, above the 0.35% cost, but the trade count is modest and the edge is unproven.','1h',1200,5,0,15.0,'WeekendThinDropReversal','2b0b509bea42ab4b0bfdf90e744397949b0c2ab8a8376ee36068d2015d5d9cd9','dropped','forbidden by the lab: leverage or margin',NULL,NULL,'2026-11-06T10:53:14.333997+00:00');
INSERT INTO "ideas" VALUES('I-021','S20261106T112143Z','Hourly MACD cross-up gated by daily MACD uptrend, exit on hourly cross-down','blog','https://quantpedia.com/how-to-design-a-simple-multi-timeframe-trend-strategy-on-bitcoin/','How to Design a Simple Multi-Timeframe Trend Strategy on Bitcoin','unknown','Hourly signals from closed 1h candles, daily trend from closed daily candles built from the 1h data (visible only after the daily close). Daily trend is up when the daily MACD line (EMA12 - EMA26 of daily closes) is above its 9-day EMA signal line. ENTRY at the close of an hourly bar when the hourly MACD line (EMA12 - EMA26 of hourly closes, signal EMA9) crosses from at-or-below to above its signal line, the daily trend is up, and no position is open; buy at next bar open. EXIT at the close of the first hourly bar where the hourly MACD line crosses below its signal line; sell at next open. Also exit if the daily trend turns down at a daily close. Hard stop 5% below entry. No other filters, no pyramiding. All MACD periods are the textbook 12/26/9.','Counterparties are slower participants who react to a daily trend with a delay: when the daily momentum is positive, an hourly momentum re-acceleration marks the continuation leg of the larger move, while the daily gate avoids buying hourly crosses inside downtrends where they are mostly noise. Holding until the hourly cross-down (not one bar) lets winners run to a few percent so the average move can exceed the 0.35% round trip; the source gives only a loose rationale (trade with the higher-timeframe trend), so this is a stated hypothesis, not proven.','1h',1000,3,1,120.0,'MultiTimeframeMACDTrend','25788274e13cef3a70811dad952aabd9116e57accba52bf1145f5457b8145a6a','registered','formalised as H-037',3.8,'H-037','2026-11-06T11:22:31.855464+00:00');
INSERT INTO "ideas" VALUES('I-022','S20261106T114433Z','Daily NR7 compression day, next-day upside breakout on 1h in 50-day uptrend','blog','https://www.luxalgo.com/library/concept/nr4-nr7-narrow-range-bars.md','NR4/NR7 Narrow-range Bars','Free to use with attribution (LuxAlgo Library)','Daily signals from closed UTC daily candles built from 1h data; execution on 1h. A day D is NR7 when its high-low range is strictly smaller than the high-low range of each of the 6 days before it. The day after D (UTC), if the last closed daily close is above the SMA(50) of daily closes, ENTRY on the first 1h bar whose close is above the NR7 day''s high (order at next 1h open), only if that bar closes before 20:00 UTC. At most one entry per NR7 day. EXIT at a 1h close below the NR7 day''s low, or after 48 1h bars from entry (time exit), whichever comes first. Hard stop at the NR7 day''s low (checked on closed bars). Enter nothing on days that are not the day after an NR7 day. No take-profit, no pyramiding.','A very narrow day means participants agreed on price and resting stop orders and breakout orders stack just beyond the range. When price clears the high, short covering and momentum buyers must buy at once, so the following move tends to exceed the narrow range. The sellers who give the money away are those who faded the range and are stopped out. The source gives no mechanism beyond compression-then-expansion; this is the closest honest one. Cost risk: the stop is the narrow range, so the target must be larger than 0.35%.','1d',50,4,1,18.0,'DailyNR7Breakout','6afa0c70e0e2c487300424849b3ea5439c4ef1d206a1c53eebdde9763589356c','registered','formalised as H-040',3.1111,'H-040','2026-11-06T11:45:55.401141+00:00');
INSERT INTO "ideas" VALUES('I-023','S20261106T114433Z','Turtle Soup on 1h: failed 20-day-low sweep reclaimed within 3 bars, buy the stop run','blog','https://www.luxalgo.com/library/concept/turtle-soup.md','Turtle Soup','Free to use with attribution (LuxAlgo Library)','Closed 1h candles only, signals at bar close, order at next bar open. Let PL = lowest low of the 480 bars (20 days) before bar t-3, and require that this low was set at least 96 bars (4 days) before bar t. SWEEP: within bars t-3..t, at least one bar low is below PL. RECLAIM: close(t) > PL and close(t-1) <= PL or the sweep occurred on bar t itself with close(t) > PL (first reclaim close only). ENTRY at close of t when sweep and reclaim hold and no position is open. Let S = the lowest low over bars t-3..t. EXIT at the first close >= the highest high of the 24 bars ending at t (target), or after 48 bars from entry, or at a close below S (stop, checked on closed bars). One entry per sweep; no re-entry for 24 bars after exit.','Stop orders of longs and breakout sellers cluster just under a well-known 20-day low. Price is pushed through, the stops trigger forced selling, and once that supply is gone and price closes back above the level, there is no follow-through, so the move snaps back. The other side is the breakout seller who sold the failed break. The source gives no evidence or mechanism beyond the pattern description; this is the closest honest one. The rebound toward the 24h high is typically several percent, above the 0.35% cost.','1h',480,5,1,25.0,'HourlyFailedBreakdownReclaim','0b1153f5e74986d152492438e675b0502c9ffd7ef546b154b6060e845264dc11','registered','formalised as H-038',3.2561,'H-038','2026-11-06T11:45:55.407803+00:00');
INSERT INTO "ideas" VALUES('I-024','S20261106T114433Z','Weekend daytime session long (Sat/Sun 13:00-21:00 UTC) when NYSE is closed, in 50-day uptrend','blog','https://quantpedia.com/are-there-seasonal-intraday-or-overnight-anomalies-in-bitcoin/','Are There Seasonal Intraday or Overnight Anomalies in Bitcoin?','unknown','UTC clock, closed 1h candles. On Saturday and Sunday only: if the last closed daily candle''s close is above the SMA(50) of daily closes (daily signal, forward-filled so only completed days are used), buy at the open of the 13:00 UTC 1h bar (14:00 bar of the US session start is 13:30 UTC in winter, so 13:00 is a fixed approximation). EXIT at the close of the 20:00 UTC bar (sell at the next open, 21:00 UTC). Hard stop 3% below entry on closed bars. Skip a day if a bar is missing. One position per pair, whole balance, no other filters.','The source reports that when the traditional market is closed, Bitcoin earns most of its return in the New York daytime hours, while on NYSE-open days the return is mostly overnight. A plausible reason is that retail and crypto-native flows are the only active buyers on weekends and hedging or arbitrage supply from equity-linked desks is absent. The other side is thin weekend sellers. Caution: the per-trade average gross move may be small compared with the 0.35% cost; the uptrend gate and stop are meant to concentrate it.','1h',1200,4,1,80.0,'WeekendDaytimeSession','cbd9acadfe3c307a0bb9a943251389cdec837abf25db1bb8e1f858dccea942e7','registered','formalised as H-039',3.2209,'H-039','2026-11-06T11:45:55.412248+00:00');
INSERT INTO "ideas" VALUES('I-025','S20261106T132940Z','Williams-style volatility breakout: day open plus 0.6 x prior-day range, 1h, flat at UTC midnight','blog','https://www.luxalgo.com/library/concept/volatility-breakout.md','Volatility Breakout (LuxAlgo Library)','Free to use with attribution','Closed 1h candles, UTC days. For each UTC day D: O = open of the 00:00 bar; R = (high - low) of day D-1 from 1h data; level = O + 0.6*R. Daily filter: close of day D-1 > SMA(50) of daily closes (50 closed days, built from 1h). ENTRY: at the close of any 1h bar from 01:00 to 18:00 UTC whose close > level, if flat and no trade already taken that day; buy at next bar open. Require R/O >= 0.02 so the trigger distance is at least 1.2%. EXIT: hard stop when a 1h close < O - 0.5*R, or at the open of the 00:00 UTC bar of the next day (time exit), whichever first. One trade per day max, no re-entry. Signals daily-derived, execution hourly.','A move of more than half of yesterday''s range beyond the open shows one-sided order flow (stop-run buying, momentum chasers, liquidations of late shorts) that tends to carry into the same day. Counterparties are sellers anchored to the open and the prior range who get run over. Requiring a wide prior range (>=2%) makes the post-trigger drift large relative to the 0.35% round trip; the day-end exit caps exposure.','1h',1200,4,0,70.0,'HourlyWilliamsVolBreakout','58853f41369ddb3bee417e410a79d92c17272f9717135e60ea52508bcab06cbd','queued','',2.1429,NULL,'2026-11-06T13:30:51.396164+00:00');
INSERT INTO "ideas" VALUES('I-026','S20261106T132940Z','Hourly inside-bar breakout of a wide mother bar, trend-filtered, midpoint invalidation','blog','https://www.luxalgo.com/library/concept/inside-bar/','Inside Bar (LuxAlgo Library)','Free to use with attribution','Closed 1h candles. Mother bar M = bar t-2, inside bar = bar t-1 when high(t-1) < high(t-2) and low(t-1) > low(t-2). Mother range must satisfy (high-low)/low >= 1.2%. Trend filter: close(t-1) > SMA(240) of 1h closes. ENTRY: the first bar t'' within the 6 bars after the inside bar whose close > mother high, if flat; buy at the next open. If no breakout in 6 bars the setup is void. EXIT: first 1h close below the mother-bar midpoint (high+low)/2, or after 24 bars from entry, whichever first. Stop: close below mother low also exits (covered by the midpoint rule). Source gives only the pattern and trend filter; the numbers here are my fixed choices.','After a large bar, a contained bar means the market digested the move without giving back ground; resting breakout stop orders and trend followers sit above the mother high. When it breaks, forced buyers (short covering, breakout chasers) pay up. Sellers on the other side are those who faded the large bar. The wide-mother-bar condition (>=1.2%) targets continuation moves larger than the 0.35% cost; the source warns many such breaks fail, so this is honest-uncertain.','1h',240,4,0,60.0,'HourlyInsideBarBreakout','d0c5b3ae00647b9ad7251bfab284ace9da2686b869cb0330b0ba6dcd7b63de88','queued','',2.2872,NULL,'2026-11-06T13:30:51.400630+00:00');
INSERT INTO "ideas" VALUES('I-027','S20261106T132940Z','Weekly anchored-VWAP reclaim: buy 1h close back above Monday-anchored VWAP in uptrend','blog','https://www.luxalgo.com/library/concept/anchored-vwap.md','Anchored VWAP (LuxAlgo Library)','Free to use with attribution','Closed 1h candles, UTC. Weekly VWAP(t) = sum(typical price*volume)/sum(volume) over bars from Monday 00:00 UTC through bar t, typical price=(high+low+close)/3. The source gives no explicit entry rule; this is my restatement of its ''reclaim of anchor'' idea. Eligible from Monday 12:00 UTC (at least 12 bars in the week). Filter: close > SMA(480) of 1h closes. SETUP: at least 8 consecutive 1h closes below VWAP, with the lowest close in that run at least 1.0% below VWAP. ENTRY: first 1h close above VWAP after the setup, buy at next open, flat only. EXIT: 1h close more than 0.7% below VWAP, or close of the Sunday 23:00 bar (week end), or 48 bars after entry. Re-anchors every Monday.','VWAP is the average cost of the week''s participants; after a sustained dip (at least 1% under it) many buyers are underwater and sell into the first retrace to break-even, but a clean reclaim means supply was absorbed and mean-reversion funds and VWAP-benchmarked execution algos buy back toward it. Counterparties are late dip sellers. The 1% depth makes the reversion distance exceed the 0.35% cost; evidence is source-light so treat as exploratory.','1h',480,5,0,40.0,'WeeklyAnchoredVWAPReclaim','51d4b218ecb401aa7371ebde7486bb11dba53dbdbbaf33003879a98da222a2f6','registered','formalised as H-041',2.2925,'H-041','2026-11-06T13:30:51.405068+00:00');
